window.READING_DATA = {"version":"2026-10-07","methods":[{"id":"S02","name":"近义词精确辨析","module_id":"S","module":"上下文词义选择","primary_count":1256,"all_link_count":1316,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师给了newest/latest个例，缺少通用辨析框架和重叠处理。","core_method":"语法合格后比较搭配强度、语域、范围和全文事实；证据不足则保留重叠，不编造差别。","decision_steps":["先用语法和搭配排除","再比较范围、语域、强度和事实","证据不足就标重叠或倾向"],"traps":["不能编造近义词禁用规则","给定答案不自动等于唯一答案"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW121:4","answer":"personal","evidence":"These personal observations指作者与自己狗相处的个人观察，随后承认可能受愿望影响；communal群体、discrete分离、absurd荒谬不合。"},{"bid":"RW13:4","answer":"equally","evidence":"equally修饰applies，列多种儿童情形表示都同样适用；equality为名词，mutually相互、equitably公平虽是副词但不如“同样适用”契合列举功能。"},{"bid":"RW395:5","answer":"deterrence","evidence":"restitution and deterrence是惩罚中的补偿与威慑目标；discipline语义更泛，endorsement/preventer不成立。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW35:1","answer":"technologies","evidence":"brain imaging technologies表示脑成像技术，methods/strategies也可描述成像方法，前文modern technology倾向technologies但不使methods不合句法。"},{"bid":"RW619:5","answer":"transforming","evidence":"给定答案“transforming”可成立，但原选项“converting, transforming, reforming, altering”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"C08","name":"固定表达与学术词块","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":647,"all_link_count":764,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师列出少量词块，需要用题库频率扩展并按结构归类。","core_method":"把完整框架作为单位记忆，如at the expense of、a great deal of、strike a balance。","decision_steps":["找空格两侧固定支点","优先识别完整框架","整体代入全文检查意义"],"traps":["背诵时保留可替换槽位","不把所有常见组合都宣称唯一"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW596:3","answer":"up","evidence":"逐项比较“out, up, to, down”后，“up”在语境“there’s always a chance that some rare or unusual bird will turn up .”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW577:4","answer":"away","evidence":"逐项比较“away, up, in, to”后，“away”在语境“may transform in response to changing times but is far from fading away .”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW95:5","answer":"prophecy","evidence":"self-fulfilling prophecy为自我实现的预言固定表达；prediction/forecast虽为预测，但固定术语是prophecy。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW534:2","answer":"in some way","evidence":"给定答案“in some way”可成立，但原选项“in no way, in some way, by the way, in some ways”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW620:8","answer":"at stake","evidence":"给定答案“at stake”可成立，但原选项“under threat, at stake, in danger, out of control”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"S04","name":"定义、类别与例项","module_id":"S","module":"上下文词义选择","primary_count":338,"all_link_count":518,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"利用定义句、同位语和列举项确定答案所属类别。","decision_steps":["找定义句、同位语和冒号列举","确定答案所属上位类别","排除类别不同的候选"],"traps":["同主题不等于同类别","例项比泛泛主题词更有力"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW553:5","answer":"drought","evidence":"逐项比较“drought, hardness, humidity, strength”后，“drought”在语境“of narrow rings means a drought .”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW408:4","answer":"compulsory","evidence":"seat belts are compulsory指法律强制使用；后文introduction of the law排除仅recommended/approved/accepted。"},{"bid":"RW393:1","answer":"substance","evidence":"a substance known as dark energy把暗能量归为某种物质/存在；matter前有a不合，asset与essence语义不符。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW619:3","answer":"experience","evidence":"给定答案“experience”可成立，但原选项“knowledge, communication, experience, conversation”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW528:3","answer":"decisiveness","evidence":"给定答案“decisiveness”可成立，但原选项“decisiveness, patience, confidence, courage”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"G04","name":"主动被动与助动词链","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":193,"all_link_count":330,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师用ing主动、ed被动作初筛，但需补充不及物动词、状态分词以及have been/can be/is being等完整链。","core_method":"先判断主语是动作发出者还是承受者，再拼完整的情态、完成、进行和被动链。","decision_steps":["判断主语是施事还是受事","保留情态/完成/进行助动词","拼出完整主动或被动链"],"traps":["ing不等于主动、ed不等于被动","by/in/with不能单独证明被动"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW580:5","answer":"conducted","evidence":"本题全文与原选项已重新核对；studies are being conducted为正在开展研究，被动进行时；abandoned放弃与继续讨论研究内容不同，culminated/confided不表达开展研究。"},{"bid":"RW393:2","answer":"detected","evidence":"can only be detected through its gravitational effects为情态被动；explored不等于由效应确认存在，founded/invented方向错误。"},{"bid":"RW580:4","answer":"passive","evidence":"本题全文与原选项已重新核对；unchosen与not actively engaged直接说明被动接收，passive；active方向反，dormant休眠、bilateral双边不描述选择方式。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW516:2","answer":"awed","evidence":"给定答案“awed”可成立，但原选项“admired, influenced, awed, appreciated”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW557:3","answer":"coined","evidence":"给定答案“coined”可成立，但原选项“discarded, coined, created, invented”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"F02","name":"词族与派生形式","module_id":"F","module":"词性、词形与名词系统","primary_count":189,"all_link_count":189,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增常见后缀与词族辨析。","core_method":"比较同词根名词、动词、形容词和副词，结合槽位及具体含义选词。","decision_steps":["找同词根候选","按槽位选名词/动词/形容词/副词","检查派生后的具体含义"],"traps":["同词根不等于同义","-ing/-ed可能是多种语法身份"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW613:1","answer":"vital","evidence":"逐项比较“vital, impressive, affordable, ordinary”后，“vital”在语境“The most vital ingredient in Indian cooking, the”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW523:5","answer":"entire","evidence":"逐项比较“entire, all, total, wholesome”后，“entire”在语境“are part of a huge circulation pattern that sends winds over the entire globe.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW509:5","answer":"absurd","evidence":"逐项比较“absurd, logical, reasonable, impractical”后，“absurd”在语境“, it would be absurd to restrict analysis of obesity, to individual greed.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW619:6","answer":"traditional","evidence":"给定答案“traditional”可成立，但原选项“regular, original, traditional, classic, altering”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW529:2","answer":"evolutionary","evidence":"给定答案“evolutionary”可成立，但原选项“biological, evolutionary, genetic, ecological”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"G07","name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":184,"all_link_count":211,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"不能仅凭后面出现by/in/with就判断ed，需要补充逻辑主语检验。","core_method":"把分词还原成关系从句，检查被修饰名词与动作的施受关系及时间关系。","decision_steps":["找分词修饰的名词","还原为关系从句","按施受和时间选择doing/done"],"traps":["别只看词尾","状态形容词与被动分词要结合意义"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW410:6","answer":"suggesting","evidence":"a study suggesting that...为现在分词后置修饰并保持审慎推断；proving过强，declaring/imposing不合科研语域。"},{"bid":"RW394:2","answer":"failing","evidence":"while failing to teach it为省略主语的分词结构，与取得进步形成反差；waiting/hesitating/hoping均不合事实。"},{"bid":"RW117:2","answer":"traveling","evidence":"birds traveling southward为向南迁飞的分词修饰，目的地是越冬地；staying/living反向静止，eating非移动。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW492:4","answer":"suggesting","evidence":"给定答案“suggesting”可成立，但原选项“suggesting, indicating, demonstrating, implying”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW679:2","answer":"confronted","evidence":"给定答案“confronted”可成立，但原选项“attached, confronted, included, compromised”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"C02","name":"形容词＋名词搭配","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":163,"all_link_count":295,"teacher_coverage":"未系统讲","teacher_gap":"新增搭配族和语境验证。","core_method":"比较修饰词与名词的惯用组合及专业语域，如substantial evidence、adverse effects。","decision_steps":["锁定名词核心","比较各形容词与该名词的常用组合","核对学术语域和褒贬方向"],"traps":["词性相同仍可能搭配强度不同","不要只凭中文都能翻通"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW59:1","answer":"complex","evidence":"复杂生物系统不太可能由巧合产生，complex engineering表达复杂设计；complimentary赞美/免费、compensatory补偿、compendious简明不支持复杂性论证。"},{"bid":"RW26:6","answer":"cavities","evidence":"nasal cavities为鼻腔，是气体释放的位置；前述noses/sinuses支持腔体，causalities/localities/infirmities不指该解剖空间。"},{"bid":"RW73:1","answer":"circular","evidence":"tables seat nine、促进围桌互动，circular圆形桌符合多人围坐；populated/perpendicular/cellular不描述这类教室桌形。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"G03","name":"主谓一致与主语核心","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":152,"all_link_count":242,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师提到单复数，但缺少主语核心、there be、百分比、集合名词和并列主语。","core_method":"删去介词短语、插入语和关系从句，找到真正主语核心；百分比和集合名词另行判断。","decision_steps":["删除介词短语和插入语","锁定主语核心及数","检查百分比、集合名词和there be"],"traps":["别让离谓语最近的名词冒充主语","and连接成分不一定组成复数主语"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW621:7","answer":"reliable","evidence":"consistent and therefore reliable说明一致使顾客可依赖品牌承诺；reputable偏声誉好，虽可与一致性相关但没有reliable直接表达兑现与可靠预期。available可获得，quality在此词性用法不自然。"},{"bid":"RW621:6","answer":"consistency","evidence":"same message、more consistent复现consistency一致性，quality/service/management为别的品牌维度，不能解释该整段重复的信息一致要求。"},{"bid":"RW667:3","answer":"contain","evidence":"逐项比较“contain, contained, containing, contains”后，“contain”在语境“to science that contain benefits for people. This high”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW677:2","answer":"characterized","evidence":"给定答案“characterized”可成立，但原选项“pocessed, characterized, opposed, tangled”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW492:3","answer":"facilitated","evidence":"给定答案“facilitated”可成立，但原选项“supported, promoted, enabled, facilitated”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"C01","name":"动词＋名词搭配","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":139,"all_link_count":258,"teacher_coverage":"未系统讲","teacher_gap":"老师仅要求积累固定搭配，需要补充可操作的搭配排除方法。","core_method":"连同宾语比较完整动作，如conduct research、meet demand、draw a conclusion。","decision_steps":["连读动词和宾语","比较英语惯用动作而非中文近义","用全文对象验证搭配"],"traps":["不要孤立背动词中文","语法正确不等于搭配自然"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW402:3","answer":"collaboration","evidence":"foster collaboration among Member States表示促进合作，与前文conflict方向相反；association/merging不如协作精确。"},{"bid":"RW416:5","answer":"knowledge","evidence":"acquiring specialist knowledge为获得专业知识；information/awareness范围不如knowledge匹配competencies。"},{"bid":"RW408:2","answer":"undermined","evidence":"undermined my confidence表示削弱信心；underestimated/understood/underwent均不与confidence构成该变化。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"F05","name":"副词位置与修饰目标","module_id":"F","module":"词性、词形与名词系统","primary_count":122,"all_link_count":138,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"明确副词修饰动词、形容词、比较级还是整句，再比较程度和态度。","decision_steps":["指出副词具体修饰谁","检查正常位置","再比较程度、时间或态度意义"],"traps":["选项全是副词时词性无效","句首副词可能修饰整句"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW243:5","answer":"actively","evidence":"actively engaging and challenging abilities，副词actively修饰并列动名词。"},{"bid":"RW449:6","answer":"positively","evidence":"received positively by contemporaries表示受到正面评价；后文still构成让步。"},{"bid":"RW441:3","answer":"intentionally","evidence":"intentionally designed to jar the visitor表示陈列被有意设计来造成冲击。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW534:1","answer":"exceptionally","evidence":"给定答案“exceptionally”可成立，但原选项“exceptionally, absolutely, completely, rarely”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW607:5","answer":"particularly","evidence":"给定答案“particularly”可成立，但原选项“specially, not to mention, particularly, despite”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"P01","name":"时间、空间与方向介词","module_id":"P","module":"介词、连接词与功能词","primary_count":111,"all_link_count":144,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"根据起点、终点、位置、范围和持续时间选择介词。","decision_steps":["确定时间/位置/方向关系","标出起点、终点、范围或持续时间","选择能表达该关系的介词"],"traps":["in/on/at不能按中文机械对应","时间点和时间段要区分"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW676:4","answer":"with","evidence":"逐项比较“with, in, upon, to”后，“with”在语境“in people’s eyes. He was also blessed with handsome looks, a”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW160:7","answer":"until","evidence":"was the longest... until completion of another bridge，until标记纪录终止点。"},{"bid":"RW552:1","answer":"for","evidence":"逐项比较“in, for, to, of”后，“for”在语境“can make life better for everyone. Engineers need to have a talent for invention and innovation, but”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW201:1","answer":"further afield","evidence":"bring in water from further afield是地道表达“从更远处”，但from distant places/remote areas/faraway locations也都可成句。"},{"bid":"RW95:4","answer":"beyond","evidence":"extends beyond the limits表示超越界限；past/outside the limits也可表达越过范围，搭配自然度有差异但语义未排尽。"}]},{"id":"D02","name":"同义复现与主题词链","module_id":"D","module":"篇章逻辑与衔接","primary_count":108,"all_link_count":202,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"追踪前后对同一对象的重复、上位词、下位词和同义替换。","decision_steps":["追踪重复词、同义词和上下位词","画出同一对象的词链","用主题连续性选择答案"],"traps":["复现不一定原词重复","局部重复不能压过全文主题"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW69:2","answer":"development","evidence":"human development后文原词复现，并展开health care、education、economic development；neglect/malevolence反向，prevalence流行不表达改善生活。"},{"bid":"RW105:2","answer":"vocalizations","evidence":"human and canine vocalizations指人犬发声，后文repeated vocal sounds/voices；sounds过泛且后面另列environmental noises，utterances偏有意义话语。"},{"bid":"RW138:3","answer":"speed","evidence":"faster communication improves speed and efficiency，speed与faster直接复现；column/rating/volume不表达运营速度。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW89:4","answer":"causes","evidence":"tested possible causes for extinction最常用；possible reasons/factors也可表达潜在成因，origins侧重起源。后文caused by复现cause但不足以证明其余全错。"},{"bid":"RW101:4","answer":"intelligence","evidence":"applying your own intelligence/knowledge/understanding to books均可表示运用认知能力；wisdom也可能。给定intelligence符合“intelligent person”复现，但不足以唯一。"}]},{"id":"C06","name":"名词＋介词配价","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":102,"all_link_count":143,"teacher_coverage":"未系统讲","teacher_gap":"新增高频名词配价表。","core_method":"核对effect on、reason for、access to等名词后的固定介词。","decision_steps":["找到名词核心","整体核对noun prep","确认介词引出对象、原因还是内容"],"traps":["不要把所有of都当所属","同义名词后介词可能不同"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW77:3","answer":"growth","evidence":"opportunities for artistic and personal growth为艺术与个人成长，daily contact和指导支持发展；image/perspective/measure不如growth承接教育收益。"},{"bid":"RW470:4","answer":"domination","evidence":"popular participation rather than elite and foreign domination形成参与民主与精英外来支配的对照。"},{"bid":"RW404:2","answer":"staple","evidence":"the staple of their diet表示饮食主食；fix/range/variety均不能表达九千年核心食物。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"D04","name":"转折、让步与反驳","module_id":"D","module":"篇章逻辑与衔接","primary_count":97,"all_link_count":241,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师列举but/however/although/while，需要补充although/while/whereas/nevertheless/on the contrary的边界。","core_method":"区分普通对照、出乎预期、承认后转折和直接反驳，再匹配连接形式。","decision_steps":["找预期与实际的冲突","区分普通对照、让步和反驳","按连接位置选择词"],"traps":["while可表时间也可表对照","on the contrary不是普通however"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW22:3","answer":"While","evidence":"While plants discovered, reptiles have also...对照植物与动物两类发现，while引完整从句；thus/however通常需不同句法，once将前句设成时点条件。"},{"bid":"RW63:2","answer":"residential","evidence":"west section后列茅草屋和住宅，与east section的businesses对照，residential说明住宅区性质。residence是住所名词，residing需有居住主体；resident虽能作形容词，但不表示这一区域以住宅为主。"},{"bid":"RW398:1","answer":"passive","evidence":"active process, not a passive one构成直接反义对照；positive/objective/proactive都不与active形成此处定义反义。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW584:1","answer":"however","evidence":"给定答案“however”可成立，但原选项“however, yet, consequently, besides”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW540:4","answer":"Although","evidence":"给定答案“Although”可成立，但原选项“While, Despite, Although, Since”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"G02","name":"时态与时间参照","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":86,"all_link_count":271,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师只列出By＋时间点，需要补充一般过去、现在完成、过去完成、机制性一般现在时及时间参照冲突。","core_method":"同时核对明确时点、持续区间、先后关系和全文叙述时间，再选择时态。","decision_steps":["圈明确时点和持续区间","确定全文叙述参照点","核对先后关系后选时态"],"traps":["by不必然等于完成时","历史人物不代表每个动词都用过去时"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW1:1","answer":"received","evidence":"has conferred报告刚发生的授予仪式，received概述该已完成事件；was receiving强调过程但这里无进行背景，had received缺明确更早过去参照，is received是人被接收而不是人获学位。"},{"bid":"RW40:6","answer":"is intruding","evidence":"whether music is intruding on desire讨论当前持续干扰，is intruding自然；完成情态形式通常表达对先前干扰的推断或反事实，本文未给该过去参照。"},{"bid":"RW480:4","answer":"intervened","evidence":"Margaret Thatcher intervened in the debate为一般过去时，并与argued/wrote平行。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW68:3","answer":"need","evidence":"need to be与ought to be都可表达安置要求，should后不能直接保留to，required现在描述单数/时态不合；need与ought不是唯一语法对立。"}]},{"id":"G11","name":"宾语、补语与使役结构","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":80,"all_link_count":91,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"识别make/keep/find/consider等后的宾语补语，判断补语应为形容词、名词、原形还是分词。","decision_steps":["先找宾语","判断后项是在命名、描述还是使其做事","选择名词/形容词/原形/分词补语"],"traps":["make sb do不带to","keep/leave/find后的补语形式不同"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW667:1","answer":"can be","evidence":"逐项比较“have, can be, has, is”后，“can be”在语境“In the rainforest, there can be more than two hundred species well”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW519:2","answer":"left","evidence":"逐项比较“took, established, left, created”后，“left”在语境“estates were divided up among all the heirs, had left France divided into many tiny farms;”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW518:5","answer":"ensure","evidence":"逐项比较“ensuring, ensures, ensure, ensured”后，“ensure”在语境“arose as a way to strengthen this maternal bond and to help ensure an infant's survival.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW593:3","answer":"disappear","evidence":"给定答案“disappear”可成立，但原选项“disservice, dissolve, dissipate, disappear”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW587:2","answer":"lacking","evidence":"给定答案“lacking”可成立，但原选项“lacking, plentiful, sufficient, absent”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"G10","name":"并列层级与共享成分","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":78,"all_link_count":225,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师提到and/but，但缺少并列层级和共享成分判断。","core_method":"圈出and/or/but/rather than连接的同级成分，确认是否共享主语、助动词、介词或to。","decision_steps":["圈and/or/but/rather than","确认连接的两端是否同级","检查共享主语、助动词、介词或to"],"traps":["形式相同不代表语义同类","as...as属于比较，不是普通并列"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW407:2","answer":"unwilling","evidence":"unwilling or unable to afford并列“不愿或无力承担”；incapable需of，eager方向相反，afraid不合。"},{"bid":"RW247:3","answer":"rather than","evidence":"rather than referring simply to adults，rather than doing表示不用笼统称呼而细分。"},{"bid":"RW609:1","answer":"both","evidence":"逐项比较“both, neither, never, almost”后，“both”在语境“Thomas Alva Edison was both a scientist and an inventor. Born in 1847, Edison would see”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW565:3","answer":"as well as","evidence":"给定答案“as well as”可成立，但原选项“in addition, as soon as, as well as, besides to”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW266:4","answer":"along with","evidence":"along with可插入主语中心成分后表示“连同”；together with、alongside、in addition to在语法和基本语义上也能成立，属于真实选项重叠。"}]},{"id":"C04","name":"动词＋介词配价","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":74,"all_link_count":142,"teacher_coverage":"未系统讲","teacher_gap":"新增高频动词配价表。","core_method":"保留动词、介词和两端对象整体记忆，如attribute A to B、result in、rely on。","decision_steps":["保留动词、介词和两端对象","写成A-动词-介词-B框架","核对及物性与后接形式"],"traps":["不要只背动词＋介词两词","to可能是介词也可能是不定式"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW401:4","answer":"samples","evidence":"match with the samples taken from crime scenes以复数samples指现场样本；specimen数不合，results/data不与taken形成此义。"},{"bid":"RW392:4","answer":"hinges on","evidence":"the success of the business hinges on successful sales表示企业成功取决于销售；leads to颠倒因果，其余搭配不成立。"},{"bid":"RW399:5","answer":"recorded","evidence":"publications are recorded in online catalogues为被登记进目录；presented不够精确，spoken/written不合。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW68:4","answer":"have","evidence":"have serious effects与cause serious effects均自然，result in serious effects也可语法成立；affect是动词不能照接effects成该意思。"},{"bid":"RW43:1","answer":"attention","evidence":"turn attention/focus from A to B均表示转向研究主题，全文没有独占attention的限制。"}]},{"id":"G05","name":"不定式及动词补语","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":74,"all_link_count":188,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师提到to do表示目的或未来，但需补充动词配价和形容词补语。","core_method":"核对控制动词和形容词要求的形式，如encourage sb to do、be likely to do、help do/to do。","decision_steps":["找到控制空格形式的动词或形容词","核对do/to do/doing配价","再判断目的或补语意义"],"traps":["to do不全是目的","need/allow/help等结构不能混用"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW667:2","answer":"known","evidence":"逐项比较“knowing, known, knew, know”后，“known”在语境“more than two hundred species well known to science that”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW82:1","answer":"helps","evidence":"noise helps them concentrate为help＋宾语＋原形；aids/assists someone to/in doing更常见，但aid/assist someone do在部分用法中可见，给定helps最自然，不能编成绝对语法禁令。"},{"bid":"RW404:1","answer":"acknowledge","evidence":"is meant to acknowledge dependence表示旨在承认依赖；remember不表达承认事实，另两项词性错误。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"C03","name":"名词＋名词术语","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":65,"all_link_count":80,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"识别学术复合名词和专业术语，判断前一个名词限定后一个名词的类别。","decision_steps":["把两个名词合成一个术语","判断前项限定的是类别/用途/材料","用全文学科主题验证"],"traps":["不要机械改成所有格或of结构","复合名词前项通常用单数但有例外"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW432:1","answer":"hereditary","evidence":"hereditary material是遗传物质术语，并由passed down from generation to generation定义。"},{"bid":"RW396:3","answer":"simulation","evidence":"computer simulation为计算机模拟，后文用算法描述星体形成；stimulation是刺激，其他项类别不符。"},{"bid":"RW152:3","answer":"rate","evidence":"unemployment rate为失业率固定搭配，large increases in the rate说明萧条特征。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"C05","name":"形容词＋介词配价","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":55,"all_link_count":64,"teacher_coverage":"未系统讲","teacher_gap":"新增高频形容词配价表。","core_method":"整体核对be responsible for、relevant to、capable of等结构及后接形式。","decision_steps":["找到形容词所描述对象","整体核对be adj prep","检查介词后接名词还是doing"],"traps":["中文“对/于/为”不能直接决定介词","同义形容词配价可能不同"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW436:3","answer":"indistinguishable","evidence":"practically indistinguishable from each other为几乎无法区分，little genetic difference提供直接证据。"},{"bid":"RW400:1","answer":"qualified","evidence":"qualified for jury service为具备陪审资格；able/capable不接for表达资格，equalled不合。"},{"bid":"RW418:6","answer":"covered","evidence":"feet are covered in skin and feathers为被覆盖状态；protected通常接by/from。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"G06","name":"动名词与介词后动作","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":55,"all_link_count":81,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师提到ing，但没有区分动名词、进行时和现在分词。","core_method":"确认to是否为介词，并检查by/of/for/without等介词后是否要求doing。","decision_steps":["先判断to/by/of/for是否为介词","介词后动作改为doing","排除进行时和分词修饰"],"traps":["used to do中的to不是介词","seeing ing不能立即判动名词"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW214:3","answer":"relying","evidence":"by presenting observations and by relying on texts，by doing平行说明论证依据。"},{"bid":"RW415:6","answer":"undertaking","evidence":"before undertaking any action中介词后doing，undertake action为正式搭配。"},{"bid":"RW426:4","answer":"by crossing","evidence":"arrived by crossing a land bridge中by后doing说明迁徙方式。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW549:4","answer":"understanding","evidence":"给定答案“understanding”可成立，但原选项“grasping, understanding, comprehending, ignoring”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"Q01","name":"比较结构与比较对象","module_id":"Q","module":"比较、数量与范围","primary_count":45,"all_link_count":151,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"识别as...as、more/less than、same as等框架，并检查两端是否比较同一维度。","decision_steps":["圈比较触发词","写出比较两端和维度","检查结构完整且对象同类"],"traps":["as...as两端缺一不可","最高级常与范围或one of连用"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW558:1","answer":"early","evidence":"逐项比较“much, early, same, late”后，“early”在语境“Roads of rails called Wagonways were being used in Germany as early as 1550. These”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW126:2","answer":"as","evidence":"books are as important as computers，同级比较首个as空缺；so/very/such不形成as...as。"},{"bid":"RW337:6","answer":"justify","evidence":"more value than any public benefit could justify表示公共收益不足以证明巨大私人资产合理。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW545:1","answer":"at least","evidence":"给定答案“at least”可成立，但原选项“at least, approximately, at most, nearly as”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW668:2","answer":"lower","evidence":"给定答案“lower”可成立，但原选项“much, lower, more, any”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"F03","name":"可数性与限定词","module_id":"F","module":"词性、词形与名词系统","primary_count":40,"all_link_count":323,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"先确定名词义项和可数性，再核对冠词、much/many、another/other等限定。","decision_steps":["先确定名词义项","判断可数/不可数","核对冠词、much/many、another/other"],"traps":["同一词不同义项可数性不同","information/evidence等不要乱加复数"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW391:5","answer":"another","evidence":"another hour and a half表示再等一个半小时；two与hour单数冲突，the other需特定两者，nothing不合句法。"},{"bid":"R16:2","answer":"anxiety","evidence":"exams looming提供焦虑来源，a limited amount of anxiety指适量焦虑，后文强调可有积极作用而非所有焦虑有害。"},{"bid":"R79:2","answer":"little","evidence":"对话有表情和互动，所以little difficulty。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW280:1","answer":"much","evidence":"much faster than expected自然，但far faster同样是标准程度副词＋比较级，全文不足以排除far。"},{"bid":"RW387:3","answer":"behavior","evidence":"sedentary behavior是常用总称；sedentary activity在此也可作不可数概念，唯一性不足。"}]},{"id":"D03","name":"因果与结果","module_id":"D","module":"篇章逻辑与衔接","primary_count":38,"all_link_count":201,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师以积极消极倾向解释因果过于粗，需要补充命题关系和语法形式。","core_method":"分别概括前后命题，判断谁解释谁，再选择because/as/therefore/lead to等形式。","decision_steps":["分别概括前后命题","判断谁解释谁","再选原因或结果的语法形式"],"traps":["积极/消极不能替代因果判断","because与because of后接结构不同"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW130:2","answer":"personalities","evidence":"behaviors and therefore personalities are learned，行为塑造人格，personalities与标题personality复现；implications等不指人的人格。"},{"bid":"RW621:3","answer":"attributed","evidence":"decline被归因于质量和服务，has been attributed to为结果归因；dedicated投入、contributed此被动框架不表结果归因，subject需subjected词形且是承受关系。"},{"bid":"RW157:1","answer":"commitments","evidence":"other commitments指工作、家庭等既有责任，解释为何需要灵活学习；options/decisions不必然妨碍学习。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW3:1","answer":"Therefore","evidence":"配乐需适合每个故事，由前述故事各异推出，因此Therefore与Accordingly都可；Because不能在这里独自后接逗号成篇章副词，However方向不合。"},{"bid":"RW294:5","answer":"Hence","evidence":"Hence表示因监管撤回农药而“因此”需要互补方法；Accordingly同样可自然表达这一结果，唯一性不足。"}]},{"id":"D01","name":"代词指代与替代","module_id":"D","module":"篇章逻辑与衔接","primary_count":36,"all_link_count":157,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"列出可能先行对象，核对数、语法功能和实际语义。","decision_steps":["列出可能先行对象","核对数、格和句法功能","检查实际语义能否回指"],"traps":["不要只找最近名词","which可回指整个前句"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW626:5","answer":"other","evidence":"逐项比较“many, other, those, these”后，“other”在语境“political reasons, some countries find it convenient to recognize or not recognize other countries.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW653:2","answer":"each other","evidence":"逐项比较“together, all, each other, another”后，“each other”在语境“by Facebook to analyze how people interact with each other online. The research showed”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW638:5","answer":"our","evidence":"逐项比较“Your, Ours, Us, Our”后，“our”在语境“an appointment to view the apartment in person. our application form is ready, and we are prepared to proceed with the”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW650:3","answer":"other","evidence":"给定答案“other”可成立，但原选项“any, some, simple, other”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"D05","name":"补充、递进与时序","module_id":"D","module":"篇章逻辑与衔接","primary_count":34,"all_link_count":108,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师提到and，但缺少moreover/in addition/subsequently/similarly等关系。","core_method":"判断后项是在新增信息、加强论点还是推进时间步骤。","decision_steps":["判断是新增、加强还是推进时间","找同层信息或时间顺序","选择对应衔接形式"],"traps":["and不能包办所有补充关系","overall是概括，不是简单递进"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW407:1","answer":"already","evidence":"already表示目前已有近三分之一来自海外，并为But now后的加大招生活动提供基线；often与比例主语不协调。"},{"bid":"RW657:2","answer":"Moreover","evidence":"逐项比较“Rather, So, Moreover, Likely”后，“Moreover”在语境“across multiple fields. Moreover , her writings emphasize the value of critical thinking. She developed a”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW422:4","answer":"Further","evidence":"Further补充盟友还提供人员与物资；Recent/Because/So不合。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW677:4","answer":"on the contrary","evidence":"给定答案“on the contrary”可成立，但原选项“however, on the contrary, in addition, on the whole”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW636:2","answer":"due to","evidence":"给定答案“due to”可成立，但原选项“depending on, as for, due to, thanks to”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"G09","name":"内容从句与疑问从句","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":34,"all_link_count":74,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"检查that/whether/how/what引出的从句是否结构完整，并判断它回答事实、选择、方式还是内容。","decision_steps":["确认从句在句中作什么成分","检查从句内部是否完整","按事实/选择/方式/内容选择引导词"],"traps":["what自身充当成分，that不充当","whether不能只按中文“是否”替换if"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW580:6","answer":"is intruding","evidence":"本题全文与原选项已重新核对；whether music is intruding on desire讨论当前持续干扰，is intruding自然；完成情态形式通常表达对先前干扰的推断或反事实，本文未给该过去参照。"},{"bid":"RW392:5","answer":"producing what","evidence":"go into producing what the sales force sells中what为融合关系结构，整体作producing的宾语；其余组合不能表达生产销售团队所售之物。"},{"bid":"RW393:4","answer":"revelation","evidence":"Copernicus's revelation that...中that从句说明揭示内容；information/message过泛，exposure不合发现义。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"Q02","name":"数量词与比例","module_id":"Q","module":"比较、数量与范围","primary_count":34,"all_link_count":68,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"根据可数性、单复数、百分比和上下限选择数量表达。","decision_steps":["确认可数性和单复数","找百分比、上下限或约数","选择数量词并核对范围"],"traps":["few/little方向偏少","number与amount对象不同"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW490:4","answer":"one","evidence":"just one type of learning表示认知学习仅是一种，后文引出另一种。"},{"bid":"RW576:5","answer":"another","evidence":"逐项比较“another, two, the other, nothing”后，“another”在语境“flight to take us. So, we waited for another hour and a half. Everyone was exhausted. No wonder we all hope”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW495:6","answer":"most","evidence":"逐项比较“the most, most, a majority, a few”后，“most”在语境“life expectancy also occurred over most of the 20th century. Unfortunately, life expectancy isn't shared across the whole”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW492:2","answer":"several","evidence":"给定答案“several”可成立，但原选项“various, several, numerous, many”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"},{"bid":"RW27:5","answer":"some","evidence":"some eighty volumes表示约80卷；almost eighty表示接近但未到80，just eighty表示仅或恰好80，projection没有足够数字条件使some唯一。mostly eighty不合直接数量修饰。"}]},{"id":"S01","name":"主体—动作—对象匹配","module_id":"S","module":"上下文词义选择","primary_count":32,"all_link_count":1734,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师只说结合上下文，需要补充三元组核对法。","core_method":"把每个选项代入完整动作，核对谁对什么做什么，排除角色或对象不匹配。","decision_steps":["写出“谁-做什么-对谁/什么”","逐项代入完整动作","排除角色、对象或动作不匹配"],"traps":["不要只翻译空格单词","搭配与事实都要成立"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW621:2","answer":"contenders","evidence":"big four与other three定位其他竞争品牌，contenders最贴市场竞争角色；members泛指成员、participants参与者、contestants参赛者不如竞争者具体。"},{"bid":"RW50:2","answer":"adopt","evidence":"adopt and start implementation为采用并实施策略，revise也可修改策略但这里设所有发展中国家的首次采用目标；rebuke/condemn责难与执行反向。"},{"bid":"RW46:4","answer":"audiences","evidence":"science outreach要寻找new audiences新受众，groups也可泛指群体但不如观众角色具体；mobs暴民、auditors审计者不指公众科普目标群体。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW621:1","answer":"claiming","evidence":"fall short of doing、未超过麦当劳并仍第二，claiming the crown表示未夺第一；winning the crown同样符合全段，getting更泛，stating较偏陈述而非夺位。"},{"bid":"RW684:3","answer":"adult","evidence":"teenage brain不是行驶里程较少的成年脑，adult最标准；grown-up也可作形容词表示成年，不能仅据搭配说错。"}]},{"id":"C07","name":"短语动词","module_id":"C","module":"固定搭配与词块","primary_count":30,"all_link_count":41,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师列举look after，但缺少短语动词识别和宾语位置方法。","core_method":"把动词与小品词整体解释，检查宾语位置和及物性，如carry out、die out、set up。","decision_steps":["把动词与小品词整体解释","检查是否可分及宾语位置","再核对时态和语态"],"traps":["代词宾语位置常受限制","字面翻译动词和副词会误判"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW111:2","answer":"blows","evidence":"urban pollution blows in and lingers表示污染随风吹入乡村并滞留；climbs/stays/strikes不能同时解释来源移动与滞留。"},{"bid":"RW418:1","answer":"up","evidence":"brighten up their black heads为使黑色头部显亮的短语动词。"},{"bid":"RW423:6","answer":"carrying","evidence":"carrying out research为开展研究的短语动词，when后接进行结构。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"G08","name":"关系从句与缺口","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":30,"all_link_count":56,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师仅把that/which当作可删除修饰，缺少关系词选择和从句缺口方法。","core_method":"找先行词，判断从句缺主语、宾语还是介词宾语，并区分限制性和非限制性从句。","decision_steps":["找到先行词","判断从句缺主语/宾语/介词宾语","区分限制性与非限制性"],"traps":["逗号后非限制性从句通常不用that","前置介词后不能随便用that"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW422:3","answer":"which","evidence":"which引非限制性关系从句，概括inclusive approach带来的加强作用。"},{"bid":"RW665:4","answer":"how much","evidence":"逐项比较“how much, how many, however, so much”后，“how much”在语境“is that farmers often do not know how much fertilizer they should use, which can lead either to poor yields or”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW519:1","answer":"whereby","evidence":"逐项比较“through, that, who, whereby”后，“whereby”在语境“attempt to introduce modern techniques from Britain had not succeeded. Inheritance laws, whereby estates were divided up among all the heirs, had”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW650:4","answer":"which","evidence":"给定答案“which”可成立，但原选项“which, then, however, as”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"P02","name":"介词短语与从句连接","module_id":"P","module":"介词、连接词与功能词","primary_count":20,"all_link_count":81,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师涉及as、yet、notwithstanding，但需系统纠正并扩展后接形式。","core_method":"区分because/because of、although/despite、during/while等后接结构。","decision_steps":["判断后面是名词性成分还是完整从句","选择介词短语或从句连接词","检查让步/原因关系"],"traps":["despite后不直接接完整主谓","because of与because不可互换"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW418:5","answer":"whilst","evidence":"whilst she goes to sea引同时发生的时间从句；meanwhile不能直接接主谓。"},{"bid":"RW454:1","answer":"As","evidence":"As Orson Welles said引出处与引语；Despite后不能直接接人加said从句。"},{"bid":"RW418:3","answer":"So that","evidence":"So that the chicks can fledge引目的从句，说明冬季繁殖的时间安排。"}],"contrast_examples":[{"bid":"RW671:3","answer":"far away","evidence":"给定答案“far away”可成立，但原选项“far away, in between, further apart, all along”中至少另有语法、搭配和语义均可代入的近义表达；题内证据不足以认证唯一。"}]},{"id":"D06","name":"条件、例外与举例","module_id":"D","module":"篇章逻辑与衔接","primary_count":16,"all_link_count":78,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"识别if/unless/provided、例外范围及for example/such as的列举关系。","decision_steps":["识别条件、必要条件、例外或举例","检查命题真值如何变化","核对连接词后接结构"],"traps":["unless等于if not但语用不同","such as后接例项而非完整结论"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW91:3","answer":"including","evidence":"The source material is wide, including...以including引出所含例项；includes会形成逗号连接的第二有限谓语且主语搭配错，included/had included时态不合。"},{"bid":"RW99:4","answer":"even","evidence":"取样地点列门框、沙发、冰箱，甚至包括自己，even强调意外的一项；without/against/unless不连接该并列列举。"},{"bid":"RW513:1","answer":"Without","evidence":"逐项比较“Without, Despite, As, With”后，“Without”在语境“Everybody needs fresh water. Without water, people, animals and plants cannot live. Although a few plants and”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"S06","name":"一词多义、比喻与专业义","module_id":"S","module":"上下文词义选择","primary_count":14,"all_link_count":183,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"用全文主题锁定义项，再核对字面动作在论证中的作用。","decision_steps":["锁定全文学科主题","列出候选词可能义项","用搭配和事实选择专业义或比喻义"],"traps":["优先义不一定是本题义","比喻必须能还原其论证作用"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW239:3","answer":"accounting","evidence":"proper accounting shows subsidies and external costs，accounting指把所有成本纳入核算。"},{"bid":"RW398:3","answer":"approach","evidence":"approach a text在此指处理/阅读文本；close、preempt、nettle均不合对象与语境。"},{"bid":"RW210:4","answer":"gulosity","evidence":"essay against gulosity，gulosity为贪食，正对应过分满足口腹。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"G12","name":"倒装、省略与特殊句式","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":13,"all_link_count":24,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"还原正常语序，识别地点倒装、比较倒装、强调句、形式it和省略结构。","decision_steps":["先还原正常语序","识别倒装触发词、形式it和省略","核对被省略成分能否从前文恢复"],"traps":["省略后仍须结构完整","强调句it不回指普通名词"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW421:1","answer":"would have","evidence":"would have a translucent quality if not for...为与现实相反的省略条件结构。"},{"bid":"RW488:7","answer":"can","evidence":"two neurons can create a mechanism表示研究揭示的能力事实，can表可能能力。"},{"bid":"RW422:1","answer":"There was","evidence":"There was引出a huge pool及随后罗马优势清单；其他选项不能建立存在结构。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"S07","name":"范围、侧重点与语域","module_id":"S","module":"上下文词义选择","primary_count":12,"all_link_count":157,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"比较整体/部分、一般/具体、正式/口语及学术领域差别，并要求上下文证据。","decision_steps":["比较整体/部分、一般/具体、正式/口语","找全文支持该差别的事实","无证据时不要硬分高下"],"traps":["词典差别不等于本文差别","语域判断需看整段"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW580:2","answer":"array","evidence":"本题全文与原选项已重新核对；a wide array of electronic devices为种类广泛的装置，array为一系列；appointment预约、access获取、arrangement布置不表示此设备范围。"},{"bid":"RW580:3","answer":"limitless","evidence":"本题全文与原选项已重新核对；limitless number强调选择大量几乎无限，wide array与遍地设备支持范围；spacious形容空间宽敞，plunging急跌，excessive强调过度虽可描述数量但非此先列可选择资源的核心。"},{"bid":"RW684:4","answer":"development","evidence":"后文fast-growing synapses与尚未连通的区域讨论脑成熟，development覆盖结构功能发展，较growth单纯增长贴切；这也是语义范围而非词性考点。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"F01","name":"句法槽位与词性","module_id":"F","module":"词性、词形与名词系统","primary_count":10,"all_link_count":51,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师提到词性排除，但需补充各种槽位的具体识别。","core_method":"根据冠词、限定词、系动词、助动词和修饰关系确定空处允许的词性，再进入语义比较。","decision_steps":["用冠词/系动词/助动词/修饰关系定槽位","排除不合词性","再做词义与搭配比较"],"traps":["词性只能初筛，不能单独定答案","冠词后可能先出现形容词"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW147:4","answer":"affordability","evidence":"affect affordability in Sydney，affordability名词作affect宾语，指住房负担能力；其余词形不合。"},{"bid":"RW439:1","answer":"individual","evidence":"individual作形容词修饰复数dictators，并由Sulla和Caesar作个体例项。"},{"bid":"R57:4","answer":"well","evidence":"after rest he will become well表示恢复健康，become＋形容词表语；well为健康的形容词。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"P03","name":"限定词、代词与功能词选择","module_id":"P","module":"介词、连接词与功能词","primary_count":10,"all_link_count":46,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"结合指代、数量和句法位置选择冠词、代词及其他功能词。","decision_steps":["确定名词是否特指及数量","检查代词回指和限定范围","再选择冠词/代词/限定词"],"traps":["some可表示“大约”","all/every/each的数与范围不同"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW490:5","answer":"certain","evidence":"certain holidays表示某些特定节日，并与specific sights/sounds对应。"},{"bid":"RW481:5","answer":"each","evidence":"elements of each回指两个opposing ideas中的每一个，并与both呼应。"},{"bid":"RW454:5","answer":"even","evidence":"America or even Europe以even加强递进，说明英国制作机制的差异范围。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"F04","name":"单复数与所有格","module_id":"F","module":"词性、词形与名词系统","primary_count":9,"all_link_count":22,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师只提单复数排除，需要补充不可数名词、复合名词和所有格。","core_method":"结合数量词、指代对象和谓语形式确定单复数及所有格。","decision_steps":["找数量词和指代对象","核对名词单复数及所有格","用谓语形式反向验证"],"traps":["复合名词的中心词决定复数","形式复数不一定语义复数"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW440:1","answer":"classes","evidence":"students in quantity food production and service management classes以复数classes概括所修课程。"},{"bid":"RW450:5","answer":"criteria","evidence":"other criteria用criterion的规范复数criteria，并由culture、method、location列举。"},{"bid":"RW412:2","answer":"variables","evidence":"independent variables与前面的dependent variable构成统计变量类别，复数由多项因素决定。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"S03","name":"变化方向与程度","module_id":"S","module":"上下文词义选择","primary_count":5,"all_link_count":235,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"圈出增减、促进、阻碍、恢复、恶化和程度词，确保答案方向一致。","decision_steps":["圈增减、促进、阻碍、恢复等方向词","确定基线与变化对象","核对答案方向和程度"],"traps":["surprisingly是态度，不一定是变化方向","比较级需明确比较基准"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"R14:1","answer":"plateaued","evidence":"After progress后说60年前plateaued达到停滞平台，后面not safer及getting worse解释进步停顿；ago定位过去式。"},{"bid":"R367:4","answer":"influence","evidence":"influence has declined表示影响力下降，Though与后文still plays a role形成让步。"},{"bid":"RW99:1","answer":"weirdest","evidence":"far stranger引出比科幻中最怪异生物更奇怪，weirdest符合最高程度；其余不描述怪异程度。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"Q03","name":"单位、尺度与范围","module_id":"Q","module":"比较、数量与范围","primary_count":3,"all_link_count":40,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"核对距离、速度、时间、比例和范围单位及其惯用表达。","decision_steps":["找数值及单位","核对速度、距离、时间或比例框架","检查单复数与介词"],"traps":["an hour是速率框架的一部分","范围表达不要遗漏起止端"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"R12:5","answer":"exceed","evidence":"some exceed 15 hours指部分学生超过建议工时上限，exceed直接接数量宾语，不加of。"},{"bid":"RW29:2","answer":"On average","evidence":"between 2 and 3 minutes为汇总通常等待时长，On average表示平均；For instance须有同类事例承接，In addition只是补充，Of course强调当然不表达统计概括。"},{"bid":"RW162:3","answer":"colonies","evidence":"five colonies of leaf-cutting ants为研究的五个蚁群，colony是蚂蚁社会单位。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"G01","name":"句子边界与有限谓语","module_id":"G","module":"句法与动词结构","primary_count":2,"all_link_count":24,"teacher_coverage":"部分讲解","teacher_gap":"老师讲了找主语和删除修饰语，但需要补充从句、并列谓语、插入语和有限谓语的准确判定。","core_method":"先划分主句、从句和并列层级，再判断空处需要有限谓语还是非谓语。不能机械使用‘一句只有一个动词’。","decision_steps":["划主句/从句/并列边界","每个分句找主语和有限谓语","再判断空处要谓语还是非谓语"],"traps":["不要套“一句只能有一个动词”","and可能连接两个谓语或两个分句"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"RW11:1","answer":"control","evidence":"and后为their proteins作主语的新分句，需有限谓语control；controlling/to control缺有限谓语，controlled虽可过去式但与are expressed及一般机制现在时不一致。"},{"bid":"RW41:3","answer":"became","evidence":"where后主语certain individuals需有限谓语became，first century BC限定过去；having become/becoming为非限定结构，become一般现在不符历史叙述。"}],"contrast_examples":[]},{"id":"S05","name":"过程阶段与结果","module_id":"S","module":"上下文词义选择","primary_count":2,"all_link_count":160,"teacher_coverage":"未讲","teacher_gap":"新增系统讲解。","core_method":"确定空处描述起因、过程、手段还是结果，避免选择同主题但阶段错误的词。","decision_steps":["把句子拆成起因/过程/手段/结果","定位空格所在阶段","排除同主题但阶段错误的词"],"traps":["原因和结果不能互换","过程名词与最终产物要分开"],"normal_examples":[{"bid":"R2:5","answer":"development","evidence":"time of development中的名词对应快速增长的突触及未连通区域，表示脑结构与功能的发展。"},{"bid":"R356:4","answer":"through","evidence":"through statistical analysis说明论证立法的手段或途径。"}],"contrast_examples":[]}],"questions":[{"practice_id":"T001","source":"RW539","type":"RW","question_id":539,"title":"Shakespeare","page":400,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"There has been a great variety of critical approach to Shakespeare's work since his death. During the 17th 【 to, or, and, but 】 18th centuries, Shakespeare was both admired and condemned. Since then, much of the adverse criticism 【 has been, will be, has not been, was not 】 considered relevant, although certain issues 【 continue, had continued, are continuing, have continued 】 to interest critics throughout the years. For instance, charges against his moral propriety were made by Samuel Johnson in the 18th century and by George Bernard Shaw in the 20th. Early criticism was directed 【 secondarily, primarily, occasionally, rarely 】 at questions of form. Shakespeare was 【 praised, commended, lauded, criticized 】 for mixing comedy and tragedy and failing to observe the unities of time and place 【 prohibited, allowed, forbidden, prescribed 】 by the rules of classical drama. Dryden and Johnson were among the critics claiming that he had 【 purified, cleaned, improved, corrupted 】 the language with false wit, puns, and ambiguity. 【 Since, Because, Despite, While 】 some of his early plays might justly be charged with a frivolous use of such devices, 20th-century criticism has tended to praise their use in later plays as adding depth and resonance of meaning.","answers":["and","has not been","have continued","primarily","criticized","prescribed","corrupted","While"],"options":["to, or, and, but","has been, will be, has not been, was not","continue, had continued, are continuing, have continued","secondarily, primarily, occasionally, rarely","praised, commended, lauded, criticized","prohibited, allowed, forbidden, prescribed","purified, cleaned, improved, corrupted","Since, Because, Despite, While"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW539:1","answer":"and","primary_point":"G10","primary_name":"并列层级与共享成分","secondary_points":["P03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“to, or, and, but”后，“and”在语境“of critical approach to Shakespeare's work since his death. During the 17th and 18th centuries, Shakespeare was both admired and condemned. Since then, much of”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW539:2","answer":"has not been","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["G03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“has been, will be, has not been, was not”后，“has not been”在语境“was both admired and condemned. Since then, much of the adverse criticism has not been considered relevant, although certain issues”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW539:3","answer":"have continued","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["G03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“continue, had continued, are continuing, have continued”后，“have continued”在语境“considered relevant, although certain issues have continued to interest critics throughout the years. For instance, charges against his moral”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW539:4","answer":"primarily","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“secondarily, primarily, occasionally, rarely”后，“primarily”在语境“and by George Bernard Shaw in the 20th. Early criticism was directed primarily at questions of form. Shakespeare was”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW539:5","answer":"criticized","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“praised, commended, lauded, criticized”后，“criticized”在语境“at questions of form. Shakespeare was criticized for mixing comedy and tragedy and failing to observe the unities of”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW539:6","answer":"prescribed","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"逐项比较“prohibited, allowed, forbidden, prescribed”后，“prescribed”在语境“and tragedy and failing to observe the unities of time and place prescribed by the rules of classical drama. Dryden and Johnson were among the”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW539:7","answer":"corrupted","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“purified, cleaned, improved, corrupted”后，“corrupted”在语境“drama. Dryden and Johnson were among the critics claiming that he had corrupted the language with false wit, puns, and ambiguity.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW539:8","answer":"While","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["P02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“Since, Because, Despite, While”后，“While”在语境“the language with false wit, puns, and ambiguity. While some of his early plays might justly be charged with a frivolous”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T002","source":"RW160","type":"RW","question_id":160,"title":"Golden Gate Bridge","page":118,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"San Francisco's Golden Gate Bridge, a stunning technological and artistic achievement, 【 opens, closes, appears, equals 】 to the public after five years of construction. 【 On, During, Since, When 】 opening day – 'Pedestrian Day' – some 200,000 bridge walkers 【 stationed, looked, marveled, laughed 】 at the 4,200-foot-long suspension bridge, which spans the Golden Gate Strait at the entrance to San Francisco Bay and 【 separates, connects, channels, differentiates 】 San Francisco and Marin County. On May 28, the Golden Gate Bridge opened to 【 aquatic, vehicular, airborne, watertight 】 traffic. On May 27, 1937, the Golden Gate Bridge was opened to great acclaim, a 【 denial, symbol, technique, yield 】 of progress in the Bay Area during a time of economic crisis. At 4,200 feet, it was the longest bridge in the world 【 since, until, along, within 】 the completion of New York City's Verrazano-Narrows Bridge in 1964. Today, the Golden Gate Bridge remains one of the world's most recognizable architectural structures.","answers":["opens","On","marveled","connects","vehicular","symbol","until"],"options":["opens, closes, appears, equals","On, During, Since, When","stationed, looked, marveled, laughed","separates, connects, channels, differentiates","aquatic, vehicular, airborne, watertight","denial, symbol, technique, yield","since, until, along, within"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW160:1","answer":"opens","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"bridge opens to the public after construction，历史叙事用现在时概述开放事件；closes方向反。"},{"bid":"RW160:2","answer":"On","primary_point":"S07","primary_name":"范围、侧重点与语域","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"On opening day表示在开放当天，On接具体日期/日子。"},{"bid":"RW160:3","answer":"marveled","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"walkers marveled at the bridge，marvel at为对壮观事物惊叹；looked需at但语气弱。"},{"bid":"RW160:4","answer":"connects","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"bridge connects San Francisco and Marin County，桥梁连接两地；separates与实际功能相反。"},{"bid":"RW160:5","answer":"vehicular","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"vehicular traffic指车辆通行，opened to vehicular traffic为桥梁开放车辆交通的常见表达。"},{"bid":"RW160:6","answer":"symbol","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"a symbol of progress把大桥视为经济危机时期的进步象征。"},{"bid":"RW160:7","answer":"until","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"was the longest... until completion of another bridge，until标记纪录终止点。"}]},{"practice_id":"T003","source":"R521","type":"R","question_id":521,"title":"Genius","page":579,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"Genius, in the popular conception, is inextricably tied up with precocity - doing something truly creative, we're inclined to think, requires the freshness and exuberance and energy of youth. Orson Welles made his masterpiece, \"Citizen Kane,\" at twenty-five. Herman Melville wrote a book a year 【 through 】 his late twenties, culminating, at age thirty-two, with \"Moby-Dick.\" Mozart wrote his breakthrough Piano Concerto No. 9 in E-Flat-Major at the 【 age 】 of twenty-one. In some creative forms, like lyric poetry, the 【 importance 】 of precocity has hardened into an iron law. How old was T. S. Eliot when he wrote \"The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock\" (\"I grow old ... I grow old\")? Twenty-three. \"Poets peak young,\" the 【 creativity 】 researcher James Kaufman maintains. Mihály Csíkszentmihályi, the author of \"Flow\", agrees: \"The most creative lyric verse is believed to be that written by the young.\" According to the Harvard psychologist Howard Gardner, a leading 【 authority 】 on creativity, \"Lyric poetry is a 【 domain 】 where 【 talent 】 is discovered early, burns brightly, and then peters out at an early age.\"","answers":["through","age","importance","creativity","authority","domain","talent"],"options":["through","age","importance","creativity","authority","domain","talent"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R521:1","answer":"through","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"给定词“through”与语境“masterpiece, \"Citizen Kane,\" at twenty-five. Herman Melville wrote a book a year through his late twenties, culminating, at age thirty-two, with \"Moby-Dick.\" Mozart wrote his”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R521:2","answer":"age","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["S06"],"evidence":"给定词“age”与语境“Mozart wrote his breakthrough Piano Concerto No. 9 in E-Flat-Major at the age of twenty-one. In some creative forms, like lyric poetry, the”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R521:3","answer":"importance","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"给定词“importance”与语境“of twenty-one. In some creative forms, like lyric poetry, the importance of precocity has hardened into an iron law. How old was T.”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R521:4","answer":"creativity","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"给定词“creativity”与语境“(\"I grow old ... I grow old\")? Twenty-three. \"Poets peak young,\" the creativity researcher James Kaufman maintains. Mihály Csíkszentmihályi, the author of \"Flow\", agrees: \"The”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R521:5","answer":"authority","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"给定词“authority”与语境“by the young.\" According to the Harvard psychologist Howard Gardner, a leading authority on creativity, \"Lyric poetry is a”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R521:6","answer":"domain","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"给定词“domain”与语境“on creativity, \"Lyric poetry is a domain where”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R521:7","answer":"talent","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"给定词“talent”与语境“where talent is discovered early, burns brightly, and then peters out at an early”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"}]},{"practice_id":"T004","source":"R2","type":"R","question_id":2,"title":"Teenage Daughter","page":1,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"Your teenage daughter gets top marks in school, captains the debate team, and volunteers at a shelter for homeless people. But while driving the family car, she text-messages her best friend and rear-ends another vehicle. How can teens be so clever, accomplished, and responsible-and reckless 【 at the same time 】 ? Easily, according to two physicians at Children's Hospital Boston and Harvard Medical School (HMS) who have been 【 exploring 】 the 【 unique 】 structure and chemistry of the 【 adolescent 】 brain. \"The teenage brain is not just an adult brain with fewer miles on it,\" says Frances E. Jensen, a professor of neurology. \"It's a paradoxical time of 【 development 】 . These are people with very 【 sharp 】 brains, but they're not quite sure what to do with them.\" Research during the past 10 years, powered by technology such as functional magnetic resonance imaging, has revealed that young brains have 【 both 】 fast-growing synapses and sections that remain unconnected.","answers":["at the same time","exploring","unique","adolescent","development","sharp","both"],"options":["at the same time","exploring","unique","adolescent","development","sharp","both"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R2:1","answer":"at the same time","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["D04"],"evidence":"负责与鲁莽同时出现，at the same time对应开头的paradox；不是把两种行为写成先后阶段。"},{"bid":"R2:2","answer":"exploring","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"have been exploring为现在完成进行结构；physicians持续研究青少年脑结构，exploring表达考察未知机制。"},{"bid":"R2:3","answer":"unique","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["F01","S02"],"evidence":"structure and chemistry为名词核心，unique修饰其特有性质；下句不是里程较少的成人脑解释这种独特性。"},{"bid":"R2:4","answer":"adolescent","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"adolescent修饰brain，全文teenagers、young brains复现青少年对象；不能只认形容词而不认年龄身份。"},{"bid":"R2:5","answer":"development","primary_point":"S05","primary_name":"过程阶段与结果","secondary_points":["C06"],"evidence":"time of development中的名词对应快速增长的突触及未连通区域，表示脑结构与功能的发展。"},{"bid":"R2:6","answer":"sharp","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S02"],"evidence":"very修饰sharp，brains为被描述对象；clever及认真学习支持思维敏锐，而后文不成熟不等于不聪明。"},{"bid":"R2:7","answer":"both","primary_point":"G10","primary_name":"并列层级与共享成分","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"have both A and B连接growing synapses与unconnected sections两个并存特征，both不能读成所有脑区已成熟。"}]},{"practice_id":"T005","source":"RW600","type":"RW","question_id":600,"title":"How World Works","page":440,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Throughout the 18th century, mathematicians, scientists and philosophers researched, discussed, and published their investigations into how the world worked, while engineers and inventors developed new and successful machines and processes. The 【 modern, newest, latest, new 】 theories inspired greater invention, and more technology encouraged theoretical scientists to make further discoveries in medicine, biology, mechanics, physics, and chemistry. By 1800, the new machines 【 have, had, has, having 】 brought revolutionary changes to the workplace, transportation and communications, and eventually to the home. Some of these inventions simply made it easier to produce things on a large scale such as textile machines and foundries, 【 that, which, when, if 】 produced large quantities of cloth and metal objects quickly and cheaply. But some inventions 【 took, completed, made, brought 】 completely new possibilities such as the first batteries, steamboats, and locomotives. It would take decades for some of these inventions 【 to make, making, make, having made 】 a big impact on the world. 【 Thus, Yet, Besides, Despite 】 their creation, and the sheer amount of imagination and risk-taking 【 involving, involve, involved, involves 】, marked the beginning of a modern, global, technologically based economy of the kind that we live in today.","answers":["latest","had","which","brought","to make","Yet","involved"],"options":["modern, newest, latest, new","have, had, has, having","that, which, when, if","took, completed, made, brought","to make, making, make, having made","Thus, Yet, Besides, Despite","involving, involve, involved, involves"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW600:1","answer":"latest","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“modern, newest, latest, new”后，“latest”在语境“while engineers and inventors developed new and successful machines and processes. The latest theories inspired greater invention, and more technology encouraged theoretical scientists to make”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW600:2","answer":"had","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“have, had, has, having”后，“had”在语境“in medicine, biology, mechanics, physics, and chemistry. By 1800, the new machines had brought revolutionary changes to the workplace, transportation and communications, and eventually to”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW600:3","answer":"which","primary_point":"G08","primary_name":"关系从句与缺口","secondary_points":["D01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“that, which, when, if”后，“which”在语境“produce things on a large scale such as textile machines and foundries, which produced large quantities of cloth and metal objects quickly and cheaply. But”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW600:4","answer":"brought","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“took, completed, made, brought”后，“brought”在语境“quantities of cloth and metal objects quickly and cheaply. But some inventions brought completely new possibilities such as the first batteries, steamboats, and locomotives. It”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW600:5","answer":"to make","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“to make, making, make, having made”后，“to make”在语境“steamboats, and locomotives. It would take decades for some of these inventions to make a big impact on the world.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW600:6","answer":"Yet","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["P02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“Thus, Yet, Besides, Despite”后，“Yet”在语境“a big impact on the world. Yet their creation, and the sheer amount of imagination and risk-taking”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW600:7","answer":"involved","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"逐项比较“involving, involve, involved, involves”后，“involved”在语境“their creation, and the sheer amount of imagination and risk-taking involved , marked the beginning of a modern, global, technologically based economy of”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T006","source":"R224","type":"R","question_id":224,"title":"Changing English","page":260,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"English has been changing throughout its lifetime and it's still changing today. For most of us, these changes are fine as long as they're well and truly in the past. Paradoxically, we can be 【 curious 】 about word origins and the stories behind the 【 structure 】 we find in our language, but we 【 experience 】 a queasy distaste for any 【 change 】 that might be happening right under our noses. There is a certain 【 lack 】 of consistency. There are even language critics who are 【 convinced 】 that English is dying, or if not dying at least being progressively 【 crippled 】 through long years of mistreatment.","answers":["curious","structure","experience","change","lack","convinced","crippled"],"options":["curious","structure","experience","change","lack","convinced","crippled"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R224:1","answer":"curious","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["C01","S01"],"evidence":"be curious about word origins为固定搭配，表示对词源感兴趣；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R224:2","answer":"structure","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"the structure we find in language指语言内部结构，承接词源和语言故事；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R224:3","answer":"experience","primary_point":"S01","primary_name":"主体—动作—对象匹配","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"experience a distaste for...表示感到厌恶，宾语为对正在发生的变化的不适；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R224:4","answer":"change","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["D04","Q01"],"evidence":"any change happening under our noses与首句language changing及过去变化形成对照；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R224:5","answer":"lack","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"a lack of consistency为固定搭配，概括人们爱研究旧变化却厌恶新变化的矛盾；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R224:6","answer":"convinced","primary_point":"G09","primary_name":"内容从句与疑问从句","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"critics who are convinced that...为be convinced that结构；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R224:7","answer":"crippled","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["S06"],"evidence":"English being progressively crippled by mistreatment用被动比喻语言遭长期损害；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"}]},{"practice_id":"T007","source":"RW49","type":"RW","question_id":49,"title":"Voting","page":34,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"When it comes to 【 depictions, elections, imperfections, valedictions 】 , sometimes we vote with our heads and sometimes with our hearts. But scientists at 【 Blundered, Stanford, Murmured, Baffled 】 say we might also be voting with our pompoms. Because they've found that our behavior at the polls is influenced by the results of local 【 sporting, gorging, poling, costing 】 events, work published in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences. Humans are emotional 【 creatures, altimeters, fajitas, daemons 】 . And our strong feelings about one thing can spread to another. So the Stanford scientists wondered whether events that are unrelated to government performance might sway the way people feel about their elected officials. And what could be less 【 immanent, bitterest, relevant, inspectorate 】 to the workings in Washington or your state capital than college football? The researchers looked at the election results from 20 years' worth of 【 presidential, dental, participle, gunmetal 】 , senatorial and gubernatorial races. And they found that a 【 cosine, quinidine, philistine, home-team 】 win before the election gave the incumbent a boost of almost two percentage points. The more beloved the team, the bigger the bounce. And it's not just football. In a separate survey, the scientists found that NCAA college basketball results affected presidential approval ratings. So next election day, you might think about practicing a little separation of stadium and state.","answers":["elections","Stanford","sporting","creatures","relevant","presidential","home-team"],"options":["depictions, elections, imperfections, valedictions","Blundered, Stanford, Murmured, Baffled","sporting, gorging, poling, costing","creatures, altimeters, fajitas, daemons","immanent, bitterest, relevant, inspectorate","presidential, dental, participle, gunmetal","cosine, quinidine, philistine, home-team"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW49:1","answer":"elections","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"vote、polls、elected officials反复说明elections选举；其他名词不指投票活动。"},{"bid":"RW49:2","answer":"Stanford","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"scientists at Stanford为机构地点，后句Stanford scientists直接复现；其余为分词或错误名词，不是此处学校专名。"},{"bid":"RW49:3","answer":"sporting","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["D02","S04"],"evidence":"后文college football、basketball复现sporting events体育赛事；gorging暴食、poling撑杆、costing成本计算不概括两种运动赛果。"},{"bid":"RW49:4","answer":"creatures","primary_point":"F04","primary_name":"单复数与所有格","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"Humans are emotional creatures把人归为有感情的生物，creatures为名词复数；altimeters测高计、fajitas食物、daemons守护精灵/程序不表示本段普通人类概念。"},{"bid":"RW49:5","answer":"relevant","primary_point":"Q01","primary_name":"比较结构与比较对象","secondary_points":["C05"],"evidence":"football与政府表现无关，less relevant to government运作支持主题；immanent内在不合相关性比较，bitterest最高级不合less，inspectorate为名词。"},{"bid":"RW49:6","answer":"presidential","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"presidential、senatorial、gubernatorial平行指总统、参议员、州长选举；dental牙科、participle分词、gunmetal合金不是政府职位。"},{"bid":"RW49:7","answer":"home-team","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"local sporting events与more beloved team说明当地home-team胜利影响现任支持；其余项是数学/药物/人群概念不描述该队伍。"}]},{"practice_id":"T008","source":"RW423","type":"RW","question_id":423,"title":"Questionnaire","page":313,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"The How I Feel About My School questionnaire, designed by experts at the University of Exeter Medical School, is 【 portable, legal, approachable, available 】 to download for free. It 【 transmits, uses, symbols, tells 】 emoticon-style faces with options of happy, ok or sad. It asks children to rate how they feel in seven situations including on the way to school, in the classroom and in the playground. It is 【 noticed, designed, influenced, consigned 】 to help teachers and others to 【 satisfy, communicate, calm, bargain 】 with very young children on complex emotions. The project was supported by the National Institute for Health Research Collaboration for Applied Health Research and Care South West Peninsula ( NIHR PenCLAHRC). Professor Tamsin Ford, Professor of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry at the University of Exeter Medical School, 【 led, received, investigated, knew 】 the design, involving children to give feedback on which style of questionnaire they could relate to best. She said: \"When we're 【 deducing, making, carrying, setting 】 out research in schools, it can be really hard to meaningfully assess how very young children are feeling. We couldn't find anything that could provide what we needed, so we decided to create something.\"","answers":["available","uses","designed","communicate","led","carrying"],"options":["portable, legal, approachable, available","transmits, uses, symbols, tells","noticed, designed, influenced, consigned","satisfy, communicate, calm, bargain","led, received, investigated, knew","deducing, making, carrying, setting"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW423:1","answer":"available","primary_point":"C05","primary_name":"形容词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G05"],"evidence":"available to download for free为可免费下载。"},{"bid":"RW423:2","answer":"uses","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"questionnaire uses emoticon-style faces表示工具采用表情图。"},{"bid":"RW423:3","answer":"designed","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["G05"],"evidence":"is designed to help为被动目的结构。"},{"bid":"RW423:4","answer":"communicate","primary_point":"C04","primary_name":"动词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"communicate with children为与儿童沟通，其他动词不接with表达该义。"},{"bid":"RW423:5","answer":"led","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"Professor Ford led the design表示主持设计。"},{"bid":"RW423:6","answer":"carrying","primary_point":"C07","primary_name":"短语动词","secondary_points":["G06"],"evidence":"carrying out research为开展研究的短语动词，when后接进行结构。"}]},{"practice_id":"T009","source":"R454","type":"R","question_id":454,"title":"Studying Law","page":507,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"It is important to 【 emphasize 】 the need for hard work as an essential part of studying law, because far too many students are tempted to think that they can succeed by relying on what they imagine to be their natural ability, without bothering to add the 【 expenditure 】 of effort. To take an analogy some people prefer the more or less instant 【 gratification 】 which comes from watching television adaptation of a classic novel to the rather more 【 laborious 】 process of reading the novel itself. Those who 【 prefer 】 watching television to reading the book are less likely to study law successfully, unless they rapidly acquire a 【 taste 】 for text-based materials .","answers":["emphasize","expenditure","gratification","laborious","prefer","taste"],"options":["emphasize","expenditure","gratification","laborious","prefer","taste"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R454:1","answer":"emphasize","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"It is important to emphasize the need...为形式主语加不定式，强调努力必要性。"},{"bid":"R454:2","answer":"expenditure","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["S06"],"evidence":"the expenditure of effort表示投入精力，延续hard work主题。"},{"bid":"R454:3","answer":"gratification","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"instant gratification from watching television表示即时满足。"},{"bid":"R454:4","answer":"laborious","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["Q01"],"evidence":"the more laborious process与instant gratification对比，读原著过程更费力。"},{"bid":"R454:5","answer":"prefer","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["C04"],"evidence":"prefer watching television to reading为prefer A to B结构。"},{"bid":"R454:6","answer":"taste","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["S06"],"evidence":"acquire a taste for text-based materials表示逐渐培养对文本材料的兴趣。"}]},{"practice_id":"T010","source":"RW418","type":"RW","question_id":418,"title":"Emperor Penguin","page":309,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"The emperor is the giant of the penguin world and the most iconic of the birds of Antarctica. Gold patches on their ears and on the top of their chest brighten 【 out, up, off, on 】 their black heads. Emperors and their closest relative, the king penguin, have unique breeding cycles, with very long chick-rearing periods. The emperor penguins breed the furthest south of any penguin species, forming large colonies on the sea-ice surrounding the Antarctic continent. They are true Antarctic birds, rarely 【 have seen, seen, had seen, seeing 】 in the subantarctic waters. 【 So that, While, However, Unless 】 the chicks can fledge in the late summer season, emperors breed during the cold, dark winter, with temperatures as low at - 50°C and winds 【 up, on, out, off 】 to 200 km per hour. They trek 50–120 km (30–75 mls) over the ice to breeding colonies which may include thousands of individuals. The female lays a single egg in May then passes it over to her mate to incubate 【 whilst, meanwhile, although, despite 】 she goes to sea to feed. For nine weeks the male fasts, losing 45% of his body weight. The male balances the egg on his feet, which are 【 covering, protected, covered, protecting 】 in a thick roll of skin and feathers. The egg can be 70°C warmer than the outside temperature.","answers":["up","seen","So that","up","whilst","covered"],"options":["out, up, off, on","have seen, seen, had seen, seeing","So that, While, However, Unless","up, on, out, off","whilst, meanwhile, although, despite","covering, protected, covered, protecting"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW418:1","answer":"up","primary_point":"C07","primary_name":"短语动词","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"brighten up their black heads为使黑色头部显亮的短语动词。"},{"bid":"RW418:2","answer":"seen","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"rarely seen in...为省略be的过去分词描述帝企鹅被见到的频率。"},{"bid":"RW418:3","answer":"So that","primary_point":"P02","primary_name":"介词短语与从句连接","secondary_points":["S05"],"evidence":"So that the chicks can fledge引目的从句，说明冬季繁殖的时间安排。"},{"bid":"RW418:4","answer":"up","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["Q03"],"evidence":"winds up to 200 km per hour为最高达到的范围表达。"},{"bid":"RW418:5","answer":"whilst","primary_point":"P02","primary_name":"介词短语与从句连接","secondary_points":["D05"],"evidence":"whilst she goes to sea引同时发生的时间从句；meanwhile不能直接接主谓。"},{"bid":"RW418:6","answer":"covered","primary_point":"C05","primary_name":"形容词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"feet are covered in skin and feathers为被覆盖状态；protected通常接by/from。"}]},{"practice_id":"T011","source":"RW289","type":"RW","question_id":289,"title":"Voter","page":212,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Researchers have 【 travelled, discovered, jostled, doubled 】 that improving voter turnout tends to result in better 【 vociferating, symbolmaking, crepitating, decision-making 】 — at least amongst fish. A recent study of 【 bark, stickleback, cask, disembark 】 found that they select a leader by consensus and, the more fish in the pool, the more likely they'll make a good choice. In the experiment, a school of fish was presented with two mock 【 reallocates, validates, commentates, candidates 】 for leader. One of the fake fish swam left, the other right. The pack of real fish was then allowed to decide which leader to follow. 【 According, Crossing, Blowing, Torquing 】 to the study, which was published recently in the journal Current Biology, the stickleback tended to follow the candidate that looked the healthiest. Larger or fatter fish, for example, were usually chosen over smaller fish. Fish with spots— often a telltale sign of disease— 【 generally, unquestionably, vigorously, imminently 】 lost out to a non-spotty adversary. The fish also seemed to have a preference for a more richly colored candidate, though the researchers say they have yet to determine why. Maybe his 【 environmental, vigil, cymbal, nonresidential 】 record won them over?","answers":["discovered","decision-making","stickleback","candidates","According","generally","environmental"],"options":["travelled, discovered, jostled, doubled","vociferating, symbolmaking, crepitating, decision-making","bark, stickleback, cask, disembark","reallocates, validates, commentates, candidates","According, Crossing, Blowing, Torquing","generally, unquestionably, vigorously, imminently","environmental, vigil, cymbal, nonresidential"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW289:1","answer":"discovered","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"Researchers have discovered that...为现在完成时引研究发现。"},{"bid":"RW289:2","answer":"decision-making","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["D03","S03","S04"],"evidence":"better decision-making概括群体投票提高选择优质领袖的结果。"},{"bid":"RW289:3","answer":"stickleback","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"a study of stickleback指对刺鱼的研究，后文school of fish复现研究对象。"},{"bid":"RW289:4","answer":"candidates","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"two mock candidates for leader指两个仿真候选领袖，与后文candidate复现。"},{"bid":"RW289:5","answer":"According","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"According to the study为固定来源短语。"},{"bid":"RW289:6","answer":"generally","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"spotted fish generally lost out表示通常而非绝对的实验趋势。"},{"bid":"RW289:7","answer":"environmental","primary_point":"S07","primary_name":"范围、侧重点与语域","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"environmental record以政治候选人的“环保政绩”双关解释颜色偏好，承接voter/candidate语域。"}]},{"practice_id":"T012","source":"RW512","type":"RW","question_id":512,"title":"Standard Language","page":380,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"At the beginning of the twenty-first century, the relationship between standard and nonstandard language is, evidently, still an uncertain one. We are at a 【 transcendent, separative, distinctive, transitional 】 point between two eras. We seem to be leaving an era when the rules of Standard English, as elected and defined by prescriptive grammarians, totally conditioned our sense of 【 notable, irreversible, acceptable, possible 】 usage, so that all other usages and varieties were considered to be inferior or corrupt, and 【 isolated, suffered, excluded, separated 】 from serious consideration. And we seem to 【 be approached, be approaching, approaching, approach 】 an era when nonstandard usages and varieties, previously denigrated or ignored, are achieving a new presence and 【 likelihood, respectability, overestimation, discrimination 】 within society, reminiscent of that found in Middle English, when dialect variation in literature was widespread and uncontentious. But we are not there 【 too, yet, neither, either 】 . The rise of Standard English has resulted in a confrontation between the standard and nonstandard dimensions of the language which has lasted for over 200 years, and this has had traumatic 【 sources, consequences, reasons, orientations 】 which will take some years to eliminate. Once people have been given an inferiority complex about the way they speak or write, they find it difficult to shake off.","answers":["transitional","acceptable","excluded","be approaching","respectability","yet","consequences"],"options":["transcendent, separative, distinctive, transitional","notable, irreversible, acceptable, possible","isolated, suffered, excluded, separated","be approached, be approaching, approaching, approach","likelihood, respectability, overestimation, discrimination","too, yet, neither, either","sources, consequences, reasons, orientations"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW512:1","answer":"transitional","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“transcendent, separative, distinctive, transitional”后，“transitional”在语境“nonstandard language is, evidently, still an uncertain one. We are at a transitional point between two eras. We seem to be leaving an era when”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW512:2","answer":"acceptable","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“notable, irreversible, acceptable, possible”后，“acceptable”在语境“as elected and defined by prescriptive grammarians, totally conditioned our sense of acceptable usage, so that all other usages and varieties were considered to be”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW512:3","answer":"excluded","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“isolated, suffered, excluded, separated”后，“excluded”在语境“other usages and varieties were considered to be inferior or corrupt, and excluded from serious consideration. And we seem to”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW512:4","answer":"be approaching","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“be approached, be approaching, approaching, approach”后，“be approaching”在语境“from serious consideration. And we seem to be approaching an era when nonstandard usages and varieties, previously denigrated or ignored, are”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW512:5","answer":"respectability","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“likelihood, respectability, overestimation, discrimination”后，“respectability”在语境“and varieties, previously denigrated or ignored, are achieving a new presence and respectability within society, reminiscent of that found in Middle English, when dialect variation”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW512:6","answer":"yet","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["P02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“too, yet, neither, either”后，“yet”在语境“variation in literature was widespread and uncontentious. But we are not there yet . The rise of Standard English has resulted in a confrontation between”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW512:7","answer":"consequences","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“sources, consequences, reasons, orientations”后，“consequences”在语境“which has lasted for over 200 years, and this has had traumatic consequences which will take some years to eliminate. Once people have been given”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T013","source":"RW148","type":"RW","question_id":148,"title":"Dark-silvery Rock","page":109,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"People in parts of western Africa and southwestern Asia were the first to realize that the dark-silvery rocks poking out of the earth could be worked into tools and weapons, sometime around 1500 B.C., evidence shows. The metal was probably discovered there 【 without, through, via, by 】 accident when some ore was dropped into a fire and cooled into wrought iron, historians think. The eureka moment didn't reach Europe for 【 the same, another, further, extra 】 500 years, traveling slowly north and west through Greece, Italy, central Europe and finally to the British Isles 【 against, with, alongside, during 】 the spread of the famous Celtic tribes. The Celts diffused iron technology over much of the continent through warfare, where their victory was assured due to the strength of iron weapons. Perhaps not the most peaceful of cultural exchanges, but where the technology did travel, it caught on fast. Iron 【 destroyed, made, enhanced, created 】 life a lot easier in those days, when just living to the age of 45 was a feat. By that time, much of Europe had settled into small village life, 【 toilled, toiling, to toil, toil 】 the soil with bronze and stone tools. Iron farming tools, such as sickles and plough tips, made the process more efficient and allowed farmers 【 exploit, to exploit, exploited, exploits 】 tougher soils, try new crops and have more time for other activities.","answers":["by","another","with","made","toiling","to exploit"],"options":["without, through, via, by","the same, another, further, extra","against, with, alongside, during","destroyed, made, enhanced, created","toilled, toiling, to toil, toil","exploit, to exploit, exploited, exploits"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW148:1","answer":"by","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["F03","P03","S01"],"evidence":"discovered by accident为偶然发现，by accident固定表达；without accident表示未出事故，through/via通常需冠词/不同表达。"},{"bid":"RW148:2","answer":"another","primary_point":"F03","primary_name":"可数性与限定词","secondary_points":["Q03","S01"],"evidence":"for another 500 years表示又过500年，another＋数量＋复数时间单位；the same/further/extra也可能表达时长但此结构叙事延迟倾向another。"},{"bid":"RW148:3","answer":"with","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"technology moved with the spread of Celtic tribes，随部落扩张传播；alongside也可表示伴随，给定with较常规但非绝对唯一。"},{"bid":"RW148:4","answer":"made","primary_point":"G11","primary_name":"宾语、补语与使役结构","secondary_points":["Q01","S03"],"evidence":"Iron made life easier，make＋宾语＋形容词比较级；enhanced需宾语如quality，created/destroyed方向不合。"},{"bid":"RW148:5","answer":"toiling","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["D05"],"evidence":"Europe had settled into village life, toiling the soil，分词补充居民耕作状态；toilled拼写错，to toil目的不如同时生活状态，toil原形冲突。"},{"bid":"RW148:6","answer":"to exploit","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"allowed farmers to exploit tougher soils，allow＋宾语＋to do；其他词形不合。"}]},{"practice_id":"T014","source":"R285","type":"R","question_id":285,"title":"Debtor","page":323,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"There isn't a financial director around who wouldn't like to 【 accelerate 】 cash flow by 【 reducing 】 debtor days- in other words, get customers to 【 pay up 】 faster. In Europe's top 1,000 quoted companies, nearly one quarter of all invoices are unpaid 【 at any point 】 in time, according to recent research carried out by the ASF organization. This means they are sitting on a total of 274 billion overdue debt. Most of this is caused by poor collection practices. According to Jan Porter, ASF's Managing Director, 'You can set up all the systems you want, you can insist on watertight contracts and payment terms, the government can even introduce late payment legislation, but there are always some debtors who fail to pay on time. Once a payment is overdue, your first step is to talk to your debtor. You should let them know the payment is late and try to find out if there is a dispute about the work, or if your debtor has financial problems. 【 This is OK 】 , but Tim Vainio, a chartered accountant, believes that too many companies are afraid of losing a relationship, and that, before 【 undertaking any action 】 , the focus should be on recovering as much money as possible, rather than on preserving a relationship.'","answers":["accelerate","reducing","pay up","at any point","This is OK","undertaking any action"],"options":["accelerate","reducing","pay up","at any point","This is OK","undertaking any action"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R285:1","answer":"accelerate","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"accelerate cash flow为加快现金回流；原词池缺失。"},{"bid":"R285:2","answer":"reducing","primary_point":"G06","primary_name":"动名词与介词后动作","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"by reducing debtor days为by＋动名词说明方法；原词池缺失。"},{"bid":"R285:3","answer":"pay up","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["G05"],"evidence":"get customers to pay up faster为get A to do及pay up短语；原词池缺失。"},{"bid":"R285:4","answer":"at any point","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"at any point in time语法相容，但金融统计更常说at any given point in time；原词池缺失，不能证明原措辞最佳。"},{"bid":"R285:5","answer":"This is OK","primary_point":"D05","primary_name":"补充、递进与时序","secondary_points":["D01","S04"],"evidence":"This is OK回指先联系债务人了解争议或财务问题这一做法；原词池缺失。"},{"bid":"R285:6","answer":"undertaking any action","primary_point":"G06","primary_name":"动名词与介词后动作","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"before undertaking any action为before＋动名词；原词池缺失。"}]},{"practice_id":"T015","source":"RW461","type":"RW","question_id":461,"title":"Investment Choice","page":343,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Men and women are making different choices about their retirement savings, which could lead to very different investment outcomes, according to Dr Claire Matthews, Director of Financial Planning at Massey University's Centre for Banking Studies. Speaking at the 2012 New Zealand Finance Colloquium, held at Massey University's Albany campus last week, Dr Matthews said demographic characteristics had a substantial impact on the choices people made about KiwiSaver funds and retirement savings more generally. 【 Apart from, In spite of, As far as, When it came to 】 fund selection, she found there were significant differences based on gender. Men are more likely to invest in aggressive and growth funds, while women are more likely to choose conservative funds. \"Males are risk takers, 【 either, only, unless, whether 】 it's in their choice of car or their investment fund,\" she says. \"But when it comes to long-term savings, risk taking can actually be an advantage.\" Dr Matthews also found that men are more likely than women to have prior savings when joining KiwiSaver. Just over half of male respondents said they had savings already, while only 38% of women did. \"These figures reflect and confirm, quite disappointingly, the difference between males and females and the level of interest they take in financial planning,\" Dr Matthews says. \"It's important for all New Zealanders to be better educated about their personal finances, but this is particularly so for women.\" Other demographic factors, including age, ethnicity, education, and income, can also influence the choices 【 being, been, have, were 】 made about retirement savings. Dr Matthews found that those with bachelor and higher degrees, and those in households with a pre- tax income of $100,000 or more, were more likely to choose aggressive and 【 retrogressive, steady, challenging, growth 】 funds. 【 To be honest, Last but not least, For example, On the other hand 】 , both the youngest and oldest age groups were more likely to be invested in 【 constructive, compensative, consecutive, conservative 】 funds. While this might be appropriate for the life- cycle stage of older investors, it might not be so appropriate for younger, longer-term investors.","answers":["When it came to","whether","being","growth","On the other hand","conservative"],"options":["Apart from, In spite of, As far as, When it came to","either, only, unless, whether","being, been, have, were","retrogressive, steady, challenging, growth","To be honest, Last but not least, For example, On the other hand","constructive, compensative, consecutive, conservative"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW461:1","answer":"When it came to","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["P02"],"evidence":"When it came to fund selection为谈到基金选择时。"},{"bid":"RW461:2","answer":"whether","primary_point":"P03","primary_name":"限定词、代词与功能词选择","secondary_points":["G09"],"evidence":"whether it's in A or B为无论在汽车还是投资基金选择中的让步范围。"},{"bid":"RW461:3","answer":"being","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"choices being made为正在作出的被动选择，分词短语作宾语补足信息。"},{"bid":"RW461:4","answer":"growth","primary_point":"C03","primary_name":"名词＋名词术语","secondary_points":["G10"],"evidence":"aggressive and growth funds为金融产品类别并列。"},{"bid":"RW461:5","answer":"On the other hand","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["D02"],"evidence":"On the other hand转向与学历收入结论不同的年龄组投资倾向。"},{"bid":"RW461:6","answer":"conservative","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["D04"],"evidence":"conservative funds与前面的aggressive and growth funds构成风险偏好对照。"}]},{"practice_id":"T016","source":"RW97","type":"RW","question_id":97,"title":"Forces of Globalization","page":71,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Forces of globalization have acted on education internationally, creating greater standardization in norms of teaching and learning. There has always been 【 considerable, countable, unforeseeable, unstable 】 similarity between schools across context: the curriculum, for example has been shown 【 being divided, to divide, to be dividing, to be divided 】 between language, mathematics, science and the arts in a comparable way in schools around the world. Likewise, school buildings in terms of their architecture share remarkable similarities internationally, 【 for a result, without a result, as a result, resulted as 】 of shared patterns of teaching and learning (although facilities and resources differ significantly.) In recent years, globalization has created increased opportunities for the 'borrowing' of education policy and practice, and 【 duplicated, exempted, generated, dispensed 】 further uniformity across national contexts. 【 Anywhere, Somewhere, Everywhere, Nowhere 】 has the internationalization of education been more apparent than in the higher education sector. The move to the internationalization of higher-education policy and practice 【 was initially driving, had initially driven, was initially driven, initially drove 】 by increased student mobility, and the desire of universities to attract students from overseas.","answers":["considerable","to be divided","as a result","generated","Nowhere","was initially driven"],"options":["considerable, countable, unforeseeable, unstable","being divided, to divide, to be dividing, to be divided","for a result, without a result, as a result, resulted as","duplicated, exempted, generated, dispensed","Anywhere, Somewhere, Everywhere, Nowhere","was initially driving, had initially driven, was initially driven, initially drove"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW97:1","answer":"considerable","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S03","F03","S01"],"evidence":"considerable similarity表示相当大的相似性，后文课程和建筑跨国相似支持程度；countable可数、unstable不稳定、unforeseeable不可预见不合。"},{"bid":"RW97:2","answer":"to be divided","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"curriculum has been shown to be divided between...为被证明分成若干领域，show A to be done；being divided等不能直接补足has been shown。"},{"bid":"RW97:3","answer":"as a result","primary_point":"D03","primary_name":"因果与结果","secondary_points":["Q01"],"evidence":"share similarities as a result of shared patterns为由于共同教学模式而相似，as a result of接名词原因；其余不构成规范原因短语。"},{"bid":"RW97:4","answer":"generated","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["D03","S05","S01"],"evidence":"borrowing policy generated further uniformity表示产生更多一致性；duplicated需宾语、exempted豁免、dispensed分配/免除不表达结果产生。"},{"bid":"RW97:5","answer":"Nowhere","primary_point":"G12","primary_name":"倒装、省略与特殊句式","secondary_points":["Q01","S01"],"evidence":"Nowhere has...been more apparent为否定/限制地点副词前置触发倒装，表示高等教育领域最明显；其他地点副词与该比较倒装意义不合。"},{"bid":"RW97:6","answer":"was initially driven","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"move was initially driven by mobility and desire为被两项因素推动，过去被动；其余主动/进行/过去完成改变施受或时间结构。"}]},{"practice_id":"T017","source":"RW449","type":"RW","question_id":449,"title":"Classic","page":333,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"One of the most important things to remember is that \"classic\" does not necessarily translate to \"favorite\" or \"bestselling\". Literature is instead considered classic when it has stood the test of time and it stands the test of time when the artistic 【 quality, facade, bid, clime 】 it expresses - be it an expression of life, truth, beauty, or anything about the universal human condition - continues to be relevant and continues to inspire emotional responses, no matter the period in which the work was 【 written, writing, write, to write 】 . Indeed, classic literature is considered as such 【 regardless of, lacking of, related with, according to 】 book sales or public popularity. That said, classic literature 【 exclusively, usually, merely, consequently 】 merits lasting recognition - from critics and other people in a position to influence such decisions - and has a universal appeal. And, while effective use of language - as well as technical excellence - is a must, not everything that is well-written or is 【 formed, characterized, notified, concluded 】 by technical achievement or critical acclaim will automatically be considered a classic. Conversely, works that have not been acknowledged or received 【 imposingly, positively, efficiently, arguably 】 by the writer's contemporaries or critics can still be considered as classics.","answers":["quality","written","regardless of","usually","characterized","positively"],"options":["quality, facade, bid, clime","written, writing, write, to write","regardless of, lacking of, related with, according to","exclusively, usually, merely, consequently","formed, characterized, notified, concluded","imposingly, positively, efficiently, arguably"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW449:1","answer":"quality","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"artistic quality表示作品表达出的艺术品质，并由life、truth、beauty例释。"},{"bid":"RW449:2","answer":"written","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"the work was written为一般过去被动，作品承受写作动作。"},{"bid":"RW449:3","answer":"regardless of","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["P02","D04"],"evidence":"regardless of book sales表示不论销量与流行度，of后接名词短语。"},{"bid":"RW449:4","answer":"usually","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["S07"],"evidence":"usually限定典型但非绝对的经典文学特征；exclusively/merely范围错误。"},{"bid":"RW449:5","answer":"characterized","primary_point":"C05","primary_name":"形容词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"be characterized by technical achievement为以技术成就为特征的被动结构。"},{"bid":"RW449:6","answer":"positively","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["C01","D04"],"evidence":"received positively by contemporaries表示受到正面评价；后文still构成让步。"}]},{"practice_id":"T018","source":"RW91","type":"RW","question_id":91,"title":"Study of Objects","page":66,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"The study of objects constitutes a relatively new field of academic enquiry, commonly 【 subject to, compared with, across from, referred to 】 as material culture studies. Students of material culture seek to understand societies, both past and present, through careful study and 【 experiment, modification, consumption, observation 】 of the physical or material objects generated by those societies. The source material for study is exceptionally wide, 【 includes, including, included, had included 】 not just human-made artefacts but also natural objects and even preserved body parts (as you saw in the film 'Encountering a body'). Some specialists in the field of material culture have made bold claims for its pre-eminence. In certain disciplines, it reigns 【 at all, supreme, everywhere, far and wide 】 . It plays a critical role in archaeology, for example, especially in circumstances where written evidence is either patchy or non-existent. 【 By no means, In such cases, In essence, In this way 】 , objects are all scholars have to rely on in forming an understanding of ancient peoples. Even where written documents survive, the physical remains of literate cultures often help to provide new and interesting insights into how people once lived and thought, 【 as long as, as if, as a result of, as in 】 the case of medieval and post-medieval archaeology. In analyzing the physical remains of societies, both past and present, historians, archaeologists, anthropologists and others have been careful to remind us that objects mean different things to different people.","answers":["referred to","observation","including","supreme","In such cases","as in"],"options":["subject to, compared with, across from, referred to","experiment, modification, consumption, observation","includes, including, included, had included","at all, supreme, everywhere, far and wide","By no means, In such cases, In essence, In this way","as long as, as if, as a result of, as in"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW91:1","answer":"referred to","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["G04","Q01"],"evidence":"commonly referred to as material culture studies为通常被称作物质文化研究，空后已有as，referred to补成refer to A as B的被动；其他短语不构成命名。"},{"bid":"RW91:2","answer":"observation","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"careful study and observation of objects表示研究并观察实物，observation与study构成学术方法；experiment需on/with且本文未写实验，modification/consumption改变或消费对象。"},{"bid":"RW91:3","answer":"including","primary_point":"D06","primary_name":"条件、例外与举例","secondary_points":["G07"],"evidence":"The source material is wide, including...以including引出所含例项；includes会形成逗号连接的第二有限谓语且主语搭配错，included/had included时态不合。"},{"bid":"RW91:4","answer":"supreme","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"reigns supreme表示占据至高地位，supreme作主语补足/方式义固定表达；其他副词短语不表达学科中的首要地位。"},{"bid":"RW91:5","answer":"In such cases","primary_point":"D05","primary_name":"补充、递进与时序","secondary_points":["D01","D06"],"evidence":"written evidence不存在的circumstances下，In such cases回指这些情形；objects成为唯一依据。其他连接语不准确回指条件。"},{"bid":"RW91:6","answer":"as in","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["D03","D06","Q01"],"evidence":"as in the case of...表示正如中世纪考古这一例；as long as条件、as if仿佛、as a result of原因均不引例。"}]},{"practice_id":"T019","source":"R101","type":"R","question_id":101,"title":"Anthropologists","page":121,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"It is commonly said by anthropologists that primitive man is 【 less 】 individual and more completely moulded by his 【 society 】 than civilized man. This contains an element of truth. Simpler societies are more 【 uniform 】 , in the sense that they call for, and provide opportunities for, a far 【 smaller 】 diversity of 【 individual 】 skills and occupations than the more complex and 【 advanced 】 societies. Increasing individualization in this sense is a necessary product of modern advanced society, and runs through all its activities from top to bottom. But it would be a serious error to set up an antithesis between this process of individualization and the growing strength and cohesion of society.","answers":["less","society","uniform","smaller","individual","advanced"],"options":["less","society","uniform","smaller","individual","advanced"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R101:1","answer":"less","primary_point":"Q01","primary_name":"比较结构与比较对象","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"less individual and more completely moulded构成less...more...对比。"},{"bid":"R101:2","answer":"society","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"moulded by his society表示个人受到所属社会塑造，by引施事。"},{"bid":"R101:3","answer":"uniform","primary_point":"Q01","primary_name":"比较结构与比较对象","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"Simpler societies are more uniform，后文较少技能与职业多样性解释更同质。"},{"bid":"R101:4","answer":"smaller","primary_point":"Q01","primary_name":"比较结构与比较对象","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"a far smaller diversity than...为比较级，far加强smaller，than引比较对象。"},{"bid":"R101:5","answer":"individual","primary_point":"G10","primary_name":"并列层级与共享成分","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"individual skills and occupations中individual修饰技能，呼应主题individualization。"},{"bid":"R101:6","answer":"advanced","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["D04","S03"],"evidence":"more complex and advanced societies与simpler societies对照，advanced说明社会发展程度。"}]},{"practice_id":"T020","source":"RW495","type":"RW","question_id":495,"title":"Life Expectancy","page":367,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Life expectancy at birth is one of the most widely used and internationally recognised indicators of population health. It focuses on the length of life 【 rather, more, none, better 】 than its quality, and provides a useful summary of the general health of the population. While an indicator describing how long Australians live that simultaneously takes into account quality of life would be a desirable summary measure of 【 density, volume, progress, surface 】 in the area, currently no such measure exists, and this is why life expectancy at birth is used as the Main Progress Indicator here. During the decade 1999 to 2009, life expectancy at birth improved for both sexes. A girl born in 2009 could expect to reach 83.9 years of age, 【 that, as, while, which 】 a boy could expect to live to 79.3 years. Over the decade, boys 'life expectancy increased 【 significantly, slightly, slowly, dramatically 】 more than girls' ( 3.1 compared with 2.1 years) . This saw the gap between the sexes' life expectancy decrease by one year to 4.6 years. In the longer term, increases 【 at, in, for, above 】 life expectancy also occurred over 【 the most, most, a majority, a few 】 of the 20th century. Unfortunately, life expectancy isn't shared across the whole population though, being lower in Tasmania and the Northern Territory, and for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.","answers":["rather","progress","while","slightly","in","most"],"options":["rather, more, none, better","density, volume, progress, surface","that, as, while, which","significantly, slightly, slowly, dramatically","at, in, for, above","the most, most, a majority, a few"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW495:1","answer":"rather","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["P02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“rather, more, none, better”后，“rather”在语境“recognised indicators of population health. It focuses on the length of life rather than its quality, and provides a useful summary of the general health”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW495:2","answer":"progress","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“density, volume, progress, surface”后，“progress”在语境“into account quality of life would be a desirable summary measure of progress in the area, currently no such measure exists, and this is why”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW495:3","answer":"while","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["P02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“that, as, while, which”后，“while”在语境“girl born in 2009 could expect to reach 83.9 years of age, while a boy could expect to live to 79.3 years. Over the decade,”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW495:4","answer":"slightly","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“significantly, slightly, slowly, dramatically”后，“slightly”在语境“to live to 79.3 years. Over the decade, boys 'life expectancy increased slightly more than girls' ( 3.1 compared with 2.1 years) . This saw”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW495:5","answer":"in","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"逐项比较“at, in, for, above”后，“in”在语境“decrease by one year to 4.6 years. In the longer term, increases in life expectancy also occurred over”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW495:6","answer":"most","primary_point":"Q02","primary_name":"数量词与比例","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“the most, most, a majority, a few”后，“most”在语境“life expectancy also occurred over most of the 20th century. Unfortunately, life expectancy isn't shared across the whole”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T021","source":"R397","type":"R","question_id":397,"title":"City Cleaner","page":446,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"Rather than 【 cringing 】 at the next beetle or wasp in your way, you might want to thank them-- for helping to keep city streets clean. Researchers from North Carolina State University working in New York City found that hungry urban arthropods play a significant role in the disposal of trash. For example, in a small section of Manhattan called the Broadway/West Street corridor, insects consume the equivalent of 60,000 hot dogs a year that would otherwise be lying in the street. And that's 【 assuming 】 the bugs stop chowing down in winter. To assess how much 【 discarded 】 food bugs got rid of, the researchers placed 【 measured 】 amounts of hot dogs, potato chips and cookies at 21 park sites and 24 street medians. Contrary to their prediction, location played an even bigger role in garbage 【 consumption 】 than biodiversity did--insects gobbled up two to three times more food in the street medians than they did in the parks. The study appears in the journal Global Change Biology. If all that garbage disposal still does not make you an arthropod admirer, then consider this: by competing with larger pests for resources, insects help keep rat populations down. There's some food for 【 thought 】 .","answers":["cringing","assuming","discarded","measured","consumption","thought"],"options":["cringing","assuming","discarded","measured","consumption","thought"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R397:1","answer":"cringing","primary_point":"C04","primary_name":"动词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G06"],"evidence":"rather than cringing at...中at为cringe配价，doing与后面的thank形成选择对照。"},{"bid":"R397:2","answer":"assuming","primary_point":"G06","primary_name":"动名词与介词后动作","secondary_points":["G09"],"evidence":"that's assuming the bugs stop...以assuming引条件假设，后接完整内容从句。"},{"bid":"R397:3","answer":"discarded","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"discarded food为被丢弃的食物，过去分词表示食物承受丢弃动作。"},{"bid":"R397:4","answer":"measured","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["G07"],"evidence":"measured amounts指预先量定的食物数量，过去分词修饰amounts。"},{"bid":"R397:5","answer":"consumption","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["Q01"],"evidence":"garbage consumption与biodiversity比较对地点效应的解释力。"},{"bid":"R397:6","answer":"thought","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["S06"],"evidence":"food for thought为值得思考之事的固定双关。"}]},{"practice_id":"T022","source":"RW90","type":"RW","question_id":90,"title":"Psychology","page":65,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Psychology as a subject of study has largely developed in the West since the late nineteenth century. During this period there has been an 【 emphasis, emphases, emphasize, emphasizing 】 on scientific thinking. Because of this, there have been many scientific studies in psychology which 【 exceed, excel, separate, explore 】 different aspects of human nature. These include studies into how biology (physical factors) influences human experience, how people use their 【 brains, feelings, minds, senses 】 (touch, taste, smell, sight and hearing) to get to know the world, how people develop, why people behave in certain ways, how memory works, how people develop language, how people understand and think about the world, what motivates people, why people have emotions and how personality develops. These scientific 【 assumptions, correlations, investigations, results 】 all contribute to an understanding of human nature. What do we mean by the practical applications of these studies? An 【 ideology, empowerment, understanding, operating 】 of psychology is useful in many different areas in life, such as education, the workplace, social services and medicine. This means that people who have knowledge of psychology can 【 register, classify, use, learn 】 or apply that knowledge in areas such as the ones listed above.","answers":["emphasis","explore","senses","investigations","understanding","use"],"options":["emphasis, emphases, emphasize, emphasizing","exceed, excel, separate, explore","brains, feelings, minds, senses","assumptions, correlations, investigations, results","ideology, empowerment, understanding, operating","register, classify, use, learn"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW90:1","answer":"emphasis","primary_point":"F03","primary_name":"可数性与限定词","secondary_points":["P03"],"evidence":"an emphasis on scientific thinking，冠词an后需单数名词emphasis；emphases复数，emphasize动词，emphasizing分词。"},{"bid":"RW90:2","answer":"explore","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["D06","S04"],"evidence":"studies explore different aspects为研究探索人性各方面，后文列举研究主题；exceed超过、excel擅长、separate分离不描述研究内容。"},{"bid":"RW90:3","answer":"senses","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"括号touch, taste, smell, sight, hearing明确列五种senses感官；brains/minds/feelings不是该枚举上位词。"},{"bid":"RW90:4","answer":"investigations","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":["D01","D03","S05"],"evidence":"These scientific investigations回指前述各项科学研究，contribute to understanding；results可指成果但前句强调studies及研究领域，不只结果。"},{"bid":"RW90:5","answer":"understanding","primary_point":"F03","primary_name":"可数性与限定词","secondary_points":["P03"],"evidence":"An understanding of psychology is useful为对心理学的理解，冠词后名词；operating分词、empowerment赋权、ideology意识形态不表达掌握知识。"},{"bid":"RW90:6","answer":"use","primary_point":"G10","primary_name":"并列层级与共享成分","secondary_points":["G04","S01"],"evidence":"can use or apply that knowledge，use与apply并列同义动作，情态can后原形；register/classify/learn不与already have knowledge的实际应用目的吻合。"}]},{"practice_id":"T023","source":"R358","type":"R","question_id":358,"title":"Effective Leaders","page":399,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"In search of lessons to 【 apply 】 in our own careers, we often try to 【 emulate 】 what effective leaders do. Roger Martin says this focus is misplaced, because moves that work in one context may make little sense in another. A more productive, though more difficult, approach is to look at how such leaders 【 think 】 . After extensive interviews with more than 50 of them, the author discovered that most are 【 integrative 】 thinkers -that is, they can hold in their heads two opposing ideas at once and then come up with a new idea that contains elements of 【 each 】 but is superior to both.","answers":["apply","emulate","think","integrative","each"],"options":["apply","emulate","think","integrative","each"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R358:1","answer":"apply","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["P01"],"evidence":"apply lessons in our careers把经验用于职业生涯，核对动作、对象和适用范围。"},{"bid":"R358:2","answer":"emulate","primary_point":"G09","primary_name":"内容从句与疑问从句","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"emulate后接what effective leaders do内容从句，表示模仿其做法。"},{"bid":"R358:3","answer":"think","primary_point":"G09","primary_name":"内容从句与疑问从句","secondary_points":["D04"],"evidence":"look at how such leaders think以how从句转向考察思维方式，而非外在动作。"},{"bid":"R358:4","answer":"integrative","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"integrative thinkers为整合型思考者，破折号后的定义解释该术语。"},{"bid":"R358:5","answer":"each","primary_point":"D01","primary_name":"代词指代与替代","secondary_points":["P03"],"evidence":"each回指前面的two opposing ideas，表示新想法包含两者各自的成分。"}]},{"practice_id":"T024","source":"R360","type":"R","question_id":360,"title":"Dark Matter","page":403,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"A new interdisciplinary centre for the study of the frontiers of the universe, from the tiniest subatomic particle to the largest chain of galaxies, has been formed at the University of Texas at Austin. The Texas Cosmology Center will be a way for the university's departments of Astronomy and Physics to 【 collaborate 】 on research that concerns them both. \"This centre will bring the two departments together in an area where they 【 overlap 】 —— in the physics of the very early universe,\" said Dr. Neal Evans, Astronomy Department chair. Astronomical observations have revealed the presence of dark matter and dark energy, 【 discoveries 】 that challenge our knowledge of fundamental physics. And today's leading theories in physics 【 involve 】 energies so high that no earthbound particle accelerator can test them. They need the universe as their 【 laboratory 】 . Dr. Steven Weinberg, Nobel laureate and professor of physics at the university, called the advent of the centre \"a very exciting development\" for that department.","answers":["collaborate","overlap","discoveries","involve","laboratory"],"options":["collaborate","overlap","discoveries","involve","laboratory"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R360:1","answer":"collaborate","primary_point":"C04","primary_name":"动词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"departments collaborate on research为部门就共同研究开展合作。"},{"bid":"R360:2","answer":"overlap","primary_point":"C04","primary_name":"动词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["D02"],"evidence":"overlap in the physics of the early universe表示两学科在该领域交叉。"},{"bid":"R360:3","answer":"discoveries","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["D02","G08"],"evidence":"discoveries概括前面的dark matter和dark energy发现，并由that关系从句继续说明。"},{"bid":"R360:4","answer":"involve","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"theories involve energies表示理论涉及极高能量，主客体关系明确。"},{"bid":"R360:5","answer":"laboratory","primary_point":"S06","primary_name":"一词多义、比喻与专业义","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"the universe as their laboratory为比喻义：宇宙充当无法在地面实现的实验场。"}]},{"practice_id":"T025","source":"RW99","type":"RW","question_id":99,"title":"Tiny Creatures","page":73,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Think of the 【 helot, weirdest, codependent, signaled 】 creatures you've ever seen in a sci-fi film. Now think of this: there are far stranger, albeit smaller, critters living in your own home. And Rob Dunn at North Carolina State University wants you to go on safari to find them. Research has been done on the 【 pattern, surface, diversity, choice 】 of bacteria, fungi and other organisms that live on our skin, in our guts, even in our belly buttons. But there are other entire ecosystems that surround us. And scientists want to understand how they differ based on how and where we live. What's the tiny life like on a door frame in Brooklyn compared with that in Des Moines? Or how do fridge 【 firestorms, cyclops, tiros, microbes 】 of an urban singleton stack up with those of a suburban family? The research team seeks ten volunteers from each state, five urban and five rural. Each volunteer will get a kit of vials and swabs, along with instructions about where and how to swipe—such as door frames, couch cushions, refrigerators, 【 without, even, against, unless 】 yourself. The samples will be 【 exempted, analyzed, clicked, forgotten 】 , to uncover the secrets of our 【 mechanic, microscopic, nondemocratic, epidemical 】 companions. To find out more, go to robdunnlab.com.","answers":["weirdest","diversity","microbes","even","analyzed","microscopic"],"options":["helot, weirdest, codependent, signaled","pattern, surface, diversity, choice","firestorms, cyclops, tiros, microbes","without, even, against, unless","exempted, analyzed, clicked, forgotten","mechanic, microscopic, nondemocratic, epidemical"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW99:1","answer":"weirdest","primary_point":"S03","primary_name":"变化方向与程度","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"far stranger引出比科幻中最怪异生物更奇怪，weirdest符合最高程度；其余不描述怪异程度。"},{"bid":"RW99:2","answer":"diversity","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"bacteria, fungi and organisms列多种生物，研究其diversity多样性；pattern也可能是分布模式，但后文不同生态系统种类支持多样性。"},{"bid":"RW99:3","answer":"microbes","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"fridge microbes指冰箱中的微生物，与tiny life、bacteria/fungi复现；其他候选不属于生物类别。"},{"bid":"RW99:4","answer":"even","primary_point":"D06","primary_name":"条件、例外与举例","secondary_points":["F05"],"evidence":"取样地点列门框、沙发、冰箱，甚至包括自己，even强调意外的一项；without/against/unless不连接该并列列举。"},{"bid":"RW99:5","answer":"analyzed","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"samples will be analyzed to uncover secrets为样本将被分析，未来被动；其他过去分词虽形式可接但语义不合研究处理。"},{"bid":"RW99:6","answer":"microscopic","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["D01","S01"],"evidence":"microscopic companions回指肉眼极小的细菌真菌，microscopic表示微观；其他形容词不描述尺寸/生物。"}]},{"practice_id":"T026","source":"RW127","type":"RW","question_id":127,"title":"Salmon","page":93,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Each fall, thousands of coho salmon flock to 【 Protect, Meant, Rebuilt, Northwest 】 rivers to spawn. But many never get the chance, especially near big cities like Seattle. \"And in some of these urban areas, up to 90 percent of the females were dying before they spawned, which is not a good thing for a population long term.\" Julann Spromberg , a toxicologist affiliated with the Northwest Fisheries Science Center. Researchers suspected these deaths were partly a matter of bad timing. The fish often reach streams during the first showers of the rainy season, which flush chemicals from roads and parking lots into the water. Now, Spromberg and her colleagues have produced the first direct evidence that this runoff kills coho salmon. Their study is in the Journal of Applied Ecology. The researchers found that fish exposed to storm water from Seattle-area highways quickly grew sick and died. Surprisingly, though, the salmon did not seem to mind taking a dip in a cocktail of common road pollutants, including 【 hydrocarbons, carcass, mothers, harness 】 and metals. That detail suggests the killer ingredient in runoff may be a different kind of chemical or a lethal combination of several 【 compounds, bloodhounds, knockouts, dropouts 】 . \"There's a whole lot of stuff in here that we haven't been able to measure or don't have the capabilities of 【 frittering, measuring, glistening, heralding 】 at this point.\" However, Spromberg says there's a way to help the fish even before scientists hunt down the culprit. Her team also found that 【 stencilling, pressuring, pensioning, filtering 】 runoff through just a few feet of soil made storm water safe for salmon. Cities can 【 polemicist, littlest, implement, dissonant 】 this simple form of clean water technology by building more systems, including roadside rain gardens, to collect runoff from paved areas and pass it through soil before it enters urban waterways. Literally a quick and dirty solution.","answers":["Northwest","hydrocarbons","compounds","measuring","filtering","implement"],"options":["Protect, Meant, Rebuilt, Northwest","hydrocarbons, carcass, mothers, harness","compounds, bloodhounds, knockouts, dropouts","frittering, measuring, glistening, heralding","stencilling, pressuring, pensioning, filtering","polemicist, littlest, implement, dissonant"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW127:1","answer":"Northwest","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":["F01"],"evidence":"Northwest rivers为美国西北部河流，后文Northwest Fisheries Center与Seattle复现区域；其余词性/意义不构成地名修饰。"},{"bid":"RW127:2","answer":"hydrocarbons","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"road pollutants包括hydrocarbons and metals，hydrocarbons为常见道路油类污染物；其余非化学污染类别。"},{"bid":"RW127:3","answer":"compounds","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"lethal combination of several compounds概括多种化学物；后句测量stuff，其他候选指动物/人群。"},{"bid":"RW127:4","answer":"measuring","primary_point":"G06","primary_name":"动名词与介词后动作","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"capabilities of measuring at this point，of介词后doing；其他分词不表示检测污染物的能力。"},{"bid":"RW127:5","answer":"filtering","primary_point":"G06","primary_name":"动名词与介词后动作","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"filtering runoff through soil made water safe，动名词短语作主语，说明土壤过滤处理。"},{"bid":"RW127:6","answer":"implement","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"Cities can implement this technology为城市可实施方案，情态后原形；其他候选不是合适动词。"}]},{"practice_id":"T027","source":"RW396","type":"RW","question_id":396,"title":"Fluid Behavior","page":292,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"If you see a movie, or a TV advertisement, that involves a fluid behaving in an unusual way, it was probably made using technology based on the work of a Monash researcher. Professor Joseph Monaghan who pioneered an influential 【 method, conspiracy, phase, deviation 】 for interpreting the behavior of liquids that underlies most special effects involving water has been 【 informed, voted, nominated, honored 】 with election to the Australian Academy of Sciences. Professor Monaghan, one of only 17 members elected in 2011, was recognized for developing the method of Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH) which has applications in the fields of astrophysics, engineering and physiology, as well as movie special effects. His research started in 1977 when he tried to use computer 【 action, stimulation, equation, simulation 】 to describe the formation of stars and stellar systems. The algorithms available at the time were 【 impossible, incapable, fallible, inapplicable 】 of describing the complicated systems that evolve out of chaotic clouds of gas in the galaxy. Professor Monaghan, and his colleague Bob Gingold, took the novel and effective approach of replacing the fluid or gas in the simulation with large numbers of particles with properties that 【 presented, showed, liked, mimicked 】 those of the fluid. SPH has become a central tool in astrophysics, where it is currently used to simulate the evolution of the universe after the Big Bang, the formation of stars, and the processes of planet building.","answers":["method","honored","simulation","incapable","mimicked"],"options":["method, conspiracy, phase, deviation","informed, voted, nominated, honored","action, stimulation, equation, simulation","impossible, incapable, fallible, inapplicable","presented, showed, liked, mimicked"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW396:1","answer":"method","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"an influential method为有影响力的方法，后文SPH明确指该方法；其余词与科研方法类别不合。"},{"bid":"RW396:2","answer":"honored","primary_point":"C04","primary_name":"动词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"was honored with election表示因当选科学院院士而获荣誉；nominated与election结果冲突，其余动词不搭配。"},{"bid":"RW396:3","answer":"simulation","primary_point":"C03","primary_name":"名词＋名词术语","secondary_points":["S05"],"evidence":"computer simulation为计算机模拟，后文用算法描述星体形成；stimulation是刺激，其他项类别不符。"},{"bid":"RW396:4","answer":"incapable","primary_point":"C05","primary_name":"形容词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G06"],"evidence":"be incapable of describing为形容词介词配价；其他形容词不能接of doing形成所需含义。"},{"bid":"RW396:5","answer":"mimicked","primary_point":"S01","primary_name":"主体—动作—对象匹配","secondary_points":["D02"],"evidence":"particle properties mimicked those of the fluid表示粒子属性模拟流体属性；those完成对应，其他动词不表达复制特征。"}]},{"practice_id":"T028","source":"RW602","type":"RW","question_id":602,"title":"Different Attainments","page":441,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"In many areas of expertise ranging from music, dance, art and literature to sports, chess, mathematics, science and foreign- language acquisition, there is abundant evidence that young people differ from one another in their attainments and in the apparent ease with which they achieve them. 【 Only, Just, Still, Even 】 within a family there may be marked differences. For example, a child who struggles at a musical instrument without 【 much, little, many, a little 】 success may be overtaken by a younger sibling. It is widely believed that the likelihood 【 to become, of become, of becoming, in becoming 】 exceptionally competent in certain fields depends on the presence or absence of inborn attributes variously labelled 'talents' or 'gifts' or less often 'natural aptitudes'. According to an informal British survey, more than three-quarters of music educators who decide 【 who, what, where, which 】 young people are to receive instruction believe that children cannot do well, unless they have special innate gifts (Davis 1994). The judgement that someone is talented is believed 【 help, helping, to help, helped 】 explain (as distinct from merely describing) that person's success. It is also widely believed that the innate talent that makes it possible for an individual to excel can be detected in early childhood.","answers":["Even","much","of becoming","which","to help"],"options":["Only, Just, Still, Even","much, little, many, a little","to become, of become, of becoming, in becoming","who, what, where, which","help, helping, to help, helped"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW602:1","answer":"Even","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“Only, Just, Still, Even”后，“Even”在语境“their attainments and in the apparent ease with which they achieve them. Even within a family there may be marked differences. For example, a child”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW602:2","answer":"much","primary_point":"Q02","primary_name":"数量词与比例","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“much, little, many, a little”后，“much”在语境“differences. For example, a child who struggles at a musical instrument without much success may be overtaken by a younger sibling. It is widely believed”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW602:3","answer":"of becoming","primary_point":"P02","primary_name":"介词短语与从句连接","secondary_points":["C04"],"evidence":"逐项比较“to become, of become, of becoming, in becoming”后，“of becoming”在语境“overtaken by a younger sibling. It is widely believed that the likelihood of becoming exceptionally competent in certain fields depends on the presence or absence of”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW602:4","answer":"which","primary_point":"G08","primary_name":"关系从句与缺口","secondary_points":["D01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“who, what, where, which”后，“which”在语境“an informal British survey, more than three-quarters of music educators who decide which young people are to receive instruction believe that children cannot do well,”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW602:5","answer":"to help","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“help, helping, to help, helped”后，“to help”在语境“innate gifts (Davis 1994). The judgement that someone is talented is believed to help explain (as distinct from merely describing) that person's success. It is also”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T029","source":"R425","type":"R","question_id":425,"title":"Country Definition","page":476,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"What is a country, and how is a country defined? When people ask how many countries there are in the world, they expect a simple answer. After 【 all 】 , we've explored the whole planet, we have international travel, satellite navigation and plenty of global organizations like the United Nations, so we 【 should 】 really know how many countries there are! However, the answer to the question varies according to whom you ask. Most people say there are 192 countries, but others point out that there could be more like 260 of them. So why isn't there a straightforward answer? The problem 【 arises 】 because there isn't a universally agreed definition of 'country' and because, for political reasons, some countries 【 find 】 it convenient to recognize or not recognize 【 other 】 countries.","answers":["all","should","arises","find","other"],"options":["all","should","arises","find","other"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R425:1","answer":"all","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["D03"],"evidence":"After all为毕竟的篇章连接语，引出理应有答案的理由。"},{"bid":"R425:2","answer":"should","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"we should know以情态动词表达合理预期。"},{"bid":"R425:3","answer":"arises","primary_point":"D03","primary_name":"因果与结果","secondary_points":["G03"],"evidence":"The problem arises because...建立问题产生原因，单数主语用arises。"},{"bid":"R425:4","answer":"find","primary_point":"G11","primary_name":"宾语、补语与使役结构","secondary_points":["G05"],"evidence":"countries find it convenient to recognize...为find＋形式宾语＋形容词补语。"},{"bid":"R425:5","answer":"other","primary_point":"P03","primary_name":"限定词、代词与功能词选择","secondary_points":["D01"],"evidence":"other countries指本国以外的国家，作recognize的对象。"}]},{"practice_id":"T030","source":"R374","type":"R","question_id":374,"title":"A Letter","page":421,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"A letter from a mother to school officials. Because her son was 【 sick 】 at home she explained his illness to them saying she did not want her son to 【 spread 】 the disease to other children. She 【 hoped 】 that the authorities would be able to 【 pass 】 on lessons to her son during this 【 period 】 .","answers":["sick","spread","hoped","pass","period"],"options":["sick","spread","hoped","pass","period"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R374:1","answer":"sick","primary_point":"F01","primary_name":"句法槽位与词性","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"her son was sick中系动词后需要状态形容词，illness进一步确认生病义。"},{"bid":"R374:2","answer":"spread","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["D03"],"evidence":"spread the disease表示把疾病传播给其他儿童，解释居家原因。"},{"bid":"R374:3","answer":"hoped","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["G09"],"evidence":"She hoped that...与整段过去叙事一致，that从句承载希望内容。"},{"bid":"R374:4","answer":"pass","primary_point":"C07","primary_name":"短语动词","secondary_points":["D01"],"evidence":"pass on lessons to her son表示把课程内容转交给他，on与pass构成短语动词。"},{"bid":"R374:5","answer":"period","primary_point":"D02","primary_name":"同义复现与主题词链","secondary_points":["Q03"],"evidence":"during this period回指儿子生病在家的这段时间。"}]},{"practice_id":"T031","source":"RW251","type":"RW","question_id":251,"title":"Scientific Method","page":186,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"The logic of the scientific method was set out by John Stuart Mill in 1843 and was 【 pointed, described, labeled, named 】 the method of difference. A simple example of what he 【 misunderstood, implied, indicated, meant 】 by this is to take two glasses of water which are identical in every 【 regard, thought, measure, respect 】 . Introduce a few drops of ink into one of these glasses. The water changes color! 【 Opposing, According, Referred, Relative 】 to Mill’s method of difference it is safe to 【 assume, doubt, believe, conclude 】 that the change in the color of the water is due to the 【 introduction, removal, incorporation, addition 】 of a new factor — the independent variable — in this case, the ink.","answers":["named","meant","respect","According","assume","introduction"],"options":["pointed, described, labeled, named","misunderstood, implied, indicated, meant","regard, thought, measure, respect","Opposing, According, Referred, Relative","assume, doubt, believe, conclude","introduction, removal, incorporation, addition"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW251:1","answer":"named","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01","C03","S04"],"evidence":"be named the method of difference表示“被命名为差异法”；labeled也有“标为”义，但正式术语命名用named更贴合。"},{"bid":"RW251:2","answer":"meant","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["D01"],"evidence":"what he meant by this为固定问法，this回指Mill提出的差异法。"},{"bid":"RW251:3","answer":"respect","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["C01","S01"],"evidence":"identical in every respect为固定搭配，表示“在各方面完全相同”。"},{"bid":"RW251:4","answer":"According","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["G05","P01"],"evidence":"According to Mill’s method为according to＋依据来源；其余选项不能组成该介词短语。"},{"bid":"RW251:5","answer":"assume","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"it is safe to assume that为常用判断框架；believe虽近义，但safe to assume更符合实验推断语气。"},{"bid":"RW251:6","answer":"introduction","primary_point":"C03","primary_name":"名词＋名词术语","secondary_points":["D02","S04","S02"],"evidence":"the introduction of a new factor与前句Introduce a few drops及实验变量术语直接照应；addition有近义空间，但搭配和复现证据均较弱。"}]},{"practice_id":"T032","source":"RW535","type":"RW","question_id":535,"title":"Global Textile Industry","page":397,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"The environmental impact of the global textile industry is hard to overstate. One-third of the water used worldwide is spent fashioning fabrics. For every ton of cloth 【 produced, produce, producing, is produced 】 , 200 tons of water is polluted with chemicals and heavy metals. An estimated 1 trillion kilowatt-hours of electricity powers the factories that card and comb, spin and weave, and cut and stitch materials into everything from T-shirts to towels, 【 leave, leaving, leaved, leaves 】 behind mountains of solid waste and a massive carbon footprint. 'Where the industry is today is not really sustainable for the long term,' says Shreyaskar Chaudhary, chief executive of Pratibha Syntex, a textile manufacturer based outside Indore, India. With something of an 'if you build it, they will come' attitude, Mr.Chaudhary has steered Pratibha 【 around, among, toward, through 】 the leading edge of eco-friendly textile production. Under his direction, Pratibha began making clothes with organic cotton in 1999. Initially, the company couldn't find enough organic farms growing cotton in central India 【 have supplied, supplying, to supply, is supplied 】 its factories. To meet production demands, Chaudhary's team had to convince conventional cotton farmers to change their growing methods. Pratibha provided seeds, cultivation instruction, and a guarantee of fair-trade prices for 【 their, its, mine, them 】 crops. Today, Pratibha has a network of 28,000 organic cotton growers across the central states of Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, and Orissa.","answers":["produced","leaving","toward","to supply","their"],"options":["produced, produce, producing, is produced","leave, leaving, leaved, leaves","around, among, toward, through","have supplied, supplying, to supply, is supplied","their, its, mine, them"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW535:1","answer":"produced","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"逐项比较“produced, produce, producing, is produced”后，“produced”在语境“water used worldwide is spent fashioning fabrics. For every ton of cloth produced , 200 tons of water is polluted with chemicals and heavy metals.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW535:2","answer":"leaving","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"逐项比较“leave, leaving, leaved, leaves”后，“leaving”在语境“weave, and cut and stitch materials into everything from T-shirts to towels, leaving behind mountains of solid waste and a massive carbon footprint. 'Where the”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW535:3","answer":"toward","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"逐项比较“around, among, toward, through”后，“toward”在语境“'if you build it, they will come' attitude, Mr.Chaudhary has steered Pratibha toward the leading edge of eco-friendly textile production. Under his direction, Pratibha began”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW535:4","answer":"to supply","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“have supplied, supplying, to supply, is supplied”后，“to supply”在语境“the company couldn't find enough organic farms growing cotton in central India to supply its factories. To meet production demands, Chaudhary's team had to convince conventional”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW535:5","answer":"their","primary_point":"D01","primary_name":"代词指代与替代","secondary_points":["D02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“their, its, mine, them”后，“their”在语境“Pratibha provided seeds, cultivation instruction, and a guarantee of fair-trade prices for their crops. Today, Pratibha has a network of 28,000 organic cotton growers across”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T033","source":"RW422","type":"RW","question_id":422,"title":"Romans","page":312,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Over many centuries and across many territories the Romans were able to win an astonishing number of military victories and their success was due to several important factors. Italy was a peninsula not easily attacked. 【 But with, There was, There is, Here has 】 a huge pool of fighting men to draw upon, a disciplined and innovative army, a centralized command and line of supply, expert engineers, effective diplomacy 【 through, by, about, and 】 a network of allies, and an inclusive approach to conquered people, 【 which, who, whom, that 】 allowed for strengthening and broadening of the Roman power and logistical bases. 【 Further, Recent, Because, So 】 , her allies not only supplied, equipped and paid for additional men but they also supplied vital materials such as grain and ships. 【 Despite of, Instead of, On top of all, At the thought of 】 this, Rome was more or less in a continuous state of war or readiness for it and believed absolutely in the necessity of defending and imposing on others what she firmly believed was her cultural superiority.","answers":["There was","through","which","Further","On top of all"],"options":["But with, There was, There is, Here has","through, by, about, and","which, who, whom, that","Further, Recent, Because, So","Despite of, Instead of, On top of all, At the thought of"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW422:1","answer":"There was","primary_point":"G12","primary_name":"倒装、省略与特殊句式","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"There was引出a huge pool及随后罗马优势清单；其他选项不能建立存在结构。"},{"bid":"RW422:2","answer":"through","primary_point":"C04","primary_name":"动词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["S05"],"evidence":"effective diplomacy through a network of allies以through说明外交实现渠道。"},{"bid":"RW422:3","answer":"which","primary_point":"G08","primary_name":"关系从句与缺口","secondary_points":["D01"],"evidence":"which引非限制性关系从句，概括inclusive approach带来的加强作用。"},{"bid":"RW422:4","answer":"Further","primary_point":"D05","primary_name":"补充、递进与时序","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"Further补充盟友还提供人员与物资；Recent/Because/So不合。"},{"bid":"RW422:5","answer":"On top of all","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["D05"],"evidence":"On top of all this为除此之外的递进表达，选项与后面的this合成完整词块。"}]},{"practice_id":"T034","source":"RW537","type":"RW","question_id":537,"title":"Spanish","page":398,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Spanish is spoken by more than 300 million people in over 20 countries and is rapidly becoming one of the most popular 【 commodities, choices, records, improvements 】 for language learners around the world. A popular course for beginners, Suenos World Spanish is designed to 【 record, meet, choose, satisfies 】 the varied needs of adult learners, 【 as, whether, nor, not 】 learning at home or in a class. From the very beginning it encourages you to develop your listening and speaking skills with confidence and 【 applies, provides, encroaches, initiates 】 many opportunities to practice reading in Spanish. Using the extensive 【 series, range, rate, wisdom 】 of media available, from the course book to the audio CDs or cassettes, to the popular accompanying television series and free online 【 actions, activities, breaches, binge 】 , Suenos World Spanish can help you reach the equivalent level of a first qualification, such as GCSE.","answers":["choices","meet","whether","provides","range","activities"],"options":["commodities, choices, records, improvements","record, meet, choose, satisfies","as, whether, nor, not","applies, provides, encroaches, initiates","series, range, rate, wisdom","actions, activities, breaches, binge"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW537:1","answer":"choices","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“commodities, choices, records, improvements”后，“choices”在语境“over 20 countries and is rapidly becoming one of the most popular choices for language learners around the world. A popular course for beginners, Suenos”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW537:2","answer":"meet","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["S06"],"evidence":"逐项比较“record, meet, choose, satisfies”后，“meet”在语境“world. A popular course for beginners, Suenos World Spanish is designed to meet the varied needs of adult learners,”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW537:3","answer":"whether","primary_point":"G09","primary_name":"内容从句与疑问从句","secondary_points":["P03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“as, whether, nor, not”后，“whether”在语境“the varied needs of adult learners, whether learning at home or in a class. From the very beginning it”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW537:4","answer":"provides","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“applies, provides, encroaches, initiates”后，“provides”在语境“encourages you to develop your listening and speaking skills with confidence and provides many opportunities to practice reading in Spanish. Using the extensive”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW537:5","answer":"range","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“series, range, rate, wisdom”后，“range”在语境“many opportunities to practice reading in Spanish. Using the extensive range of media available, from the course book to the audio CDs or”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW537:6","answer":"activities","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“actions, activities, breaches, binge”后，“activities”在语境“CDs or cassettes, to the popular accompanying television series and free online activities , Suenos World Spanish can help you reach the equivalent level of”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T035","source":"RW478","type":"RW","question_id":478,"title":"Online Campus","page":355,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Remember when universities were bursting at the seams with students sitting in the aisles, balancing books on their knees? No more, it seems. E-learning is as likely to stand for empty lecture theatres as for the internet 【 revolution, period, change, time 】 , which has greatly increased the 【 price, volume, resilience, hyperbole 】 and range of course materials available online in the past five years. \" The 【 interest, temptation, frustration, trigger 】 now is to simply think, 'Everything will be online so I don't need to go to class',\" said Dr Kerri-Lee Krause, of the Centre for the Study of Higher Education at the University of Melbourne. The nation's universities are in the process of opening the doors for the new academic year and, while classes are generally well 【 designed, placed, participated, attended 】 for the early weeks, it often does not last. \" There is concern at the university level about student attendance dropping and why students are not coming to lectures,\"Dr Krause said. But lecturers' pride - and 【 intensive, less, fierce, brutal 】 competition among universities for students - mean few are willing to acknowledge publicly how poorly attended many classes are.","answers":["revolution","volume","temptation","attended","fierce"],"options":["revolution, period, change, time","price, volume, resilience, hyperbole","interest, temptation, frustration, trigger","designed, placed, participated, attended","intensive, less, fierce, brutal"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW478:1","answer":"revolution","primary_point":"C03","primary_name":"名词＋名词术语","secondary_points":["S06"],"evidence":"internet revolution指互联网带来的教学变革。"},{"bid":"RW478:2","answer":"volume","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["Q02","S03"],"evidence":"increase the volume and range of materials表示提高在线材料数量和范围。"},{"bid":"RW478:3","answer":"temptation","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G05"],"evidence":"temptation is to simply think...表示容易产生不去上课的想法。"},{"bid":"RW478:4","answer":"attended","primary_point":"C05","primary_name":"形容词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G04"],"evidence":"classes are well attended为课程出席率高的被动/状态表达。"},{"bid":"RW478:5","answer":"fierce","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"fierce competition among universities为高校间激烈竞争。"}]},{"practice_id":"T036","source":"RW494","type":"RW","question_id":494,"title":"Debt, Poverty and Development","page":366,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Books and articles highlighting intractable debt, poverty and development abound in both the academic and popular literature. This addition to the debate is both timely and interesting 【 that, as, so, whereas 】 it subsumes the economic debate to the broader social, political, environmental and institutional context of debt in developing countries. Debt-for-Development Exchanges: History and New Applications 【 has intended, intends, is intending, is intended 】 for a wide audience including: academics from a range of disciplines (including accounting and finance); non-Government organizations (NGOs); civil society groups; and, both debtor and creditor governments and public sector organization. Professor Ross Buckley, author and editor, 【 develops, has developed, have developed, developed 】 an international profile in the area of debt relief and this book is the outcome of an Australian Research Council (ARC) Discovery grant to explore debt-for development mechanisms that relieve debt, improve development outcomes 【 to, for, from, as 】 aid, are practically and politically attractive to creditors and 【 contribution, contributed, contributing, contribute 】 to regional security.","answers":["as","is intended","has developed","from","contribute"],"options":["that, as, so, whereas","has intended, intends, is intending, is intended","develops, has developed, have developed, developed","to, for, from, as","contribution, contributed, contributing, contribute"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW494:1","answer":"as","primary_point":"D05","primary_name":"补充、递进与时序","secondary_points":["D04"],"evidence":"逐项比较“that, as, so, whereas”后，“as”在语境“popular literature. This addition to the debate is both timely and interesting as it subsumes the economic debate to the broader social, political, environmental and”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW494:2","answer":"is intended","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["G03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“has intended, intends, is intending, is intended”后，“is intended”在语境“context of debt in developing countries. Debt-for-Development Exchanges: History and New Applications is intended for a wide audience including: academics from a range of disciplines (including”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW494:3","answer":"has developed","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["G03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“develops, has developed, have developed, developed”后，“has developed”在语境“creditor governments and public sector organization. Professor Ross Buckley, author and editor, has developed an international profile in the area of debt relief and this book”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW494:4","answer":"from","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"逐项比较“to, for, from, as”后，“from”在语境“grant to explore debt-for development mechanisms that relieve debt, improve development outcomes from aid, are practically and politically attractive to creditors and”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW494:5","answer":"contribute","primary_point":"G10","primary_name":"并列层级与共享成分","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"逐项比较“contribution, contributed, contributing, contribute”后，“contribute”在语境“aid, are practically and politically attractive to creditors and contribute to regional security.”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T037","source":"RW432","type":"RW","question_id":432,"title":"DNA","page":320,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"DNA is a molecule that does two things. First, it acts as the 【 acquired, familial, nutritional, hereditary 】 material, which is passed down from generation to generation. Second, it directs, to a considerable extent, the construction of our bodies, telling our cells what kinds of molecules to make and 【 establishing, guiding, pushing, determining 】 our development from a single-celled zygote to a fully formed adult. These two things are of course 【 supplanted, connected, paralleled, required 】 . The DNA sequences that construct the best bodies are more likely to get passed down to the next generation because well-constructed bodies are more likely to survive and 【 thus, yet, namely, nevertheless 】 to reproduce. This is Darwin's theory of natural selection stated in the language of DNA.","answers":["hereditary","guiding","connected","thus"],"options":["acquired, familial, nutritional, hereditary","establishing, guiding, pushing, determining","supplanted, connected, paralleled, required","thus, yet, namely, nevertheless"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW432:1","answer":"hereditary","primary_point":"C03","primary_name":"名词＋名词术语","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"hereditary material是遗传物质术语，并由passed down from generation to generation定义。"},{"bid":"RW432:2","answer":"guiding","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["G10"],"evidence":"guiding our development与前面的telling our cells平行，表示DNA引导发育。"},{"bid":"RW432:3","answer":"connected","primary_point":"S01","primary_name":"主体—动作—对象匹配","secondary_points":["D03"],"evidence":"遗传信息与身体构建两项功能因自然选择而相互关联，connected概括后文因果。"},{"bid":"RW432:4","answer":"thus","primary_point":"D03","primary_name":"因果与结果","secondary_points":["P03"],"evidence":"thus表示良好构造的个体更可能存活，因而更可能繁殖。"}]},{"practice_id":"T038","source":"R408","type":"R","question_id":408,"title":"Egg-eating Snakes","page":457,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"Egg-eating snakes are a small group of snakes whose 【 diet 】 consists only of eggs. Some eat only small eggs, which they have to swallow 【 whole 】 , as the snake has no teeth. Instead, some other snakes eat bigger eggs, but it requires special 【 treatment 】 . These snakes have spines that stick 【 out 】 from the backbone. The spines crack the egg 【 open 】 as it passes through the throat.","answers":["diet","whole","treatment","out","open"],"options":["diet","whole","treatment","out","open"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R408:1","answer":"diet","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["G08"],"evidence":"diet consists of eggs中whose关系从句说明蛇的饮食构成。"},{"bid":"R408:2","answer":"whole","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["S07"],"evidence":"swallow eggs whole中whole作宾补/状态补语，表示整颗吞下。"},{"bid":"R408:3","answer":"treatment","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S05"],"evidence":"special treatment指处理大蛋所需的特殊机制，后文脊椎突起解释。"},{"bid":"R408:4","answer":"out","primary_point":"C07","primary_name":"短语动词","secondary_points":["P01"],"evidence":"stick out from the backbone为从脊柱突出。"},{"bid":"R408:5","answer":"open","primary_point":"G11","primary_name":"宾语、补语与使役结构","secondary_points":["S05"],"evidence":"crack the egg open为动词＋宾语＋结果补语。"}]},{"practice_id":"T039","source":"RW412","type":"RW","question_id":412,"title":"Overseas Departures","page":304,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Over the past ten years, Australian overseas departures have grown from 1.7 million to 3.2 million. This represents strong average, annual growth of 6.5 per cent. This paper 【 increases, encouraged, analyses, decreases 】 outbound travel demand to each destination country using the travel demand models of short- term resident departures. The models are specified in terms of a double logarithmic linear functional form, with overseas departures as the dependent variable and real household disposable income prices of travel and accommodation in Australia and overseas and the exchange rate as independent 【 variability, variables, varies, variety 】 . The models were estimated using historical time series data from 1973 to 1998. The data were obtained from several 【 resources, sources, websites, journals 】 such as the World Tourism Organization, Australian Bureau of Statistics, World Bank and International Monetary Fund. The results suggest that the estimated elasticity parameters are consistent with standard economic theory. The number of short-term resident departures is positively influenced by per capita real household disposable income, and the price of domestic travel and accommodation, and 【 negativism, negatively, negative, negation, negated 】 influenced by the price of travel and accommodation overseas. The estimated demand models were used to develop the Tourism Forecasting Council’s long run forecasts. The forecasts suggest that the number of short- term resident departures will increase strongly over the next ten years, largely due to the strength of the Australian economy, competitive travel prices, and Australians' interest in 【 experiencing, employed, experimenting, explaining 】 different cultures and lifestyles.","answers":["analyses","variables","sources","negatively","experiencing"],"options":["increases, encouraged, analyses, decreases","variability, variables, varies, variety","resources, sources, websites, journals","negativism, negatively, negative, negation, negated","experiencing, employed, experimenting, explaining"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW412:1","answer":"analyses","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["G03"],"evidence":"This paper analyses demand中paper为单数主语，analyses作动词表示分析。"},{"bid":"RW412:2","answer":"variables","primary_point":"F04","primary_name":"单复数与所有格","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"independent variables与前面的dependent variable构成统计变量类别，复数由多项因素决定。"},{"bid":"RW412:3","answer":"sources","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["D06"],"evidence":"several sources由WTO、ABS、World Bank等机构例举。"},{"bid":"RW412:4","answer":"negatively","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["G10"],"evidence":"positively influenced与negatively influenced平行，副词修饰被动分词。"},{"bid":"RW412:5","answer":"experiencing","primary_point":"G06","primary_name":"动名词与介词后动作","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"interest in experiencing cultures中介词in后接动名词。"}]},{"practice_id":"T040","source":"R380","type":"R","question_id":380,"title":"Insect Concealment","page":426,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"The world of species is tricky, in which it is often 【 fatal 】 for insects to be exposed, and they have to 【 conceal 】 themselves in order to survive. For predators, nothing is less 【 appetizing 】 than what appears to be a dead prey. This camouflage mechanism only 【 works 】 effectively when the insect stays completely still, often remaining hidden 【 until 】 the danger has passed.","answers":["fatal","conceal","appetizing","works","until"],"options":["fatal","conceal","appetizing","works","until"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R380:1","answer":"fatal","primary_point":"C05","primary_name":"形容词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["D03"],"evidence":"it is fatal for insects to be exposed中fatal for表示暴露对昆虫可致命。"},{"bid":"R380:2","answer":"conceal","primary_point":"G11","primary_name":"宾语、补语与使役结构","secondary_points":["G05","D01"],"evidence":"have to conceal themselves使用反身宾语，表示昆虫必须隐藏自己。"},{"bid":"R380:3","answer":"appetizing","primary_point":"Q01","primary_name":"比较结构与比较对象","secondary_points":["S02"],"evidence":"nothing is less appetizing than dead prey用less...than比较捕食吸引力。"},{"bid":"R380:4","answer":"works","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["S05"],"evidence":"mechanism为单数主语用works，条件从句说明机制生效条件。"},{"bid":"R380:5","answer":"until","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["D05"],"evidence":"until the danger has passed标记保持静止的时间终点。"}]},{"practice_id":"T041","source":"R547","type":"R","question_id":547,"title":"Sex-biased Hiring","page":610,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"Discrimination against women has been alleged in hiring practices for many occupations, but it is extremely difficult to demonstrate sex-biased hiring. A change 【 in 】 the way symphony orchestras 【 recruit 】 musicians provides an unusual way to test for sex-biased hiring. To overcome possible biases in hiring, most orchestras 【 revised 】 their audition policies in the 1970s and 1980s. A major change involved the use of 'blind' auditions with a 'screen' to 【 conceal 】 the identity of the candidate from the jury. Female musicians in the top five symphony orchestras in the United States were less than 5% of all players in 1970 but are 25% today. We ask whether women were more likely to be advanced and/or hired with the use of 'blind' auditions. Using data from actual auditions in an individual fixed-effects framework, we find that the screen 【 increases 】 by 50% the probability a woman will be 【 advanced 】 out of certain preliminary rounds. The screen also enhances, by several fold, the likelihood a female contestant will be the winner in the final round. Using data on orchestra personnel, the switch to 'blind' auditions can explain between 30% and 55% of the increase in the proportion female among new hires and between 25% and 46% of the increase in the percentage female in the orchestras since 1970.","answers":["in","recruit","revised","conceal","increases","advanced"],"options":["in","recruit","revised","conceal","increases","advanced"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R547:1","answer":"in","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"同文同空答案：复用RW51:1；不认证R原词池唯一。a change in the way...为招聘方式的变化，in引变化所在方面；around/beyond/by不表达同样常用关系。"},{"bid":"R547:2","answer":"recruit","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"给定词“recruit”与语境“the way symphony orchestras recruit musicians provides an unusual way to test for sex-biased hiring. To overcome”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R547:3","answer":"revised","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"给定词“revised”与语境“test for sex-biased hiring. To overcome possible biases in hiring, most orchestras revised their audition policies in the 1970s and 1980s. A major change involved”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R547:4","answer":"conceal","primary_point":"S01","primary_name":"主体—动作—对象匹配","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"同文同空答案：复用RW51:2；不认证R原词池唯一。blind auditions with screen为遮住身份防偏见，conceal identity符合目的；contain容纳、cancel取消、check核查都不表示让评审不知道身份。"},{"bid":"R547:5","answer":"increases","primary_point":"G03","primary_name":"主谓一致与主语核心","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"给定词“increases”与语境“actual auditions in an individual fixed-effects framework, we find that the screen increases by 50% the probability a woman will be”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R547:6","answer":"advanced","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["G02"],"evidence":"给定词“advanced”与语境“by 50% the probability a woman will be advanced out of certain preliminary rounds. The screen also enhances, by several fold,”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"}]},{"practice_id":"T042","source":"RW29","type":"RW","question_id":29,"title":"UK Drivers","page":19,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"In the UK, it is recommended that drivers should turn off their car engines when they expect to be stationary for more than 1 minute. To encourage drivers 【 to turn off, turn off, turning off, turned off 】 their engines while waiting at rail crossings, the Kent city council placed a permanent sign at the crossing asking drivers to \"please switch off your engine when barriers are down to help improve air quality.\" 【 For instance, On average, In addition, Of course 】 , drivers had to wait between 2 and 3 minutes to cross after the barrier had gone down. However, the sign didn't seem to be convincing the 【 exception, minority, majority, unity 】 of drivers to switch off their engines. \" 【 Although, Since, Because, Thus 】 some research suggests that signs 【 alone, lonely, neither, either 】 can change behavior, the message on this sign was designed simply to be an informational request and was not guided by any particular behavioral theory,\" the researchers explain. So the research team, led by Rose Mellady of the University of East Anglia, designed an intervention study.","answers":["to turn off","On average","majority","Although","alone"],"options":["to turn off, turn off, turning off, turned off","For instance, On average, In addition, Of course","exception, minority, majority, unity","Although, Since, Because, Thus","alone, lonely, neither, either"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW29:1","answer":"to turn off","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["G11"],"evidence":"encourage drivers to turn off为encourage＋人＋to do，其余三种动词形式不能直接接此宾补。"},{"bid":"RW29:2","answer":"On average","primary_point":"Q03","primary_name":"单位、尺度与范围","secondary_points":["C08","D05","D06"],"evidence":"between 2 and 3 minutes为汇总通常等待时长，On average表示平均；For instance须有同类事例承接，In addition只是补充，Of course强调当然不表达统计概括。"},{"bid":"RW29:3","answer":"majority","primary_point":"Q02","primary_name":"数量词与比例","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"sign didn’t seem convincing the majority说明大多数未被说服，后文研究干预以改善；minority语法可通但改变效力评价，全文未给实际比例，勿当数量形式唯一。"},{"bid":"RW29:4","answer":"Although","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["D03","P02"],"evidence":"some research suggests signs change behavior是正面预期，但本标牌只是无理论的信息请求，Although引出让步；Since/Because变原因，Thus不能直接引从属句。"},{"bid":"RW29:5","answer":"alone","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"signs alone表示单凭标牌，alone后置强调；lonely表示孤独，neither/either不能单独后置于signs表示仅仅。"}]},{"practice_id":"T043","source":"RW463","type":"RW","question_id":463,"title":"Nightjar","page":345,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"When you spend your days nesting on the ground and weigh less than 100 grams, self-preservation depends on mastering the art of disguise. The nightjar's soft plumage and variegated coloring help it 【 blending, blend, blended, blends 】 in with its surrounds, but it is the bird's own judgement in choosing the most sympathetic background that 【 pleads, makes, wins, changes 】 it a camouflage champion. Each bird chooses where to nest 【 based, basing, basis, basic 】 on its specific patterns and colors, says camouflage researcher Martin Stevens, of the Centre for Ecology and Conservation at the University of Exeter in Cornwall. \"Each individual bird looks a little bit different,\" he says. \"This is not a species-level choice. Individual birds consistently sit in places that enhance their own unique markings, 【 together, both, either, whether 】 within a habitat and at a fine scale with regards to specific background sites.\"","answers":["blend","makes","based","both"],"options":["blending, blend, blended, blends","pleads, makes, wins, changes","based, basing, basis, basic","together, both, either, whether"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW463:1","answer":"blend","primary_point":"G11","primary_name":"宾语、补语与使役结构","secondary_points":["C07"],"evidence":"help it blend in为help＋宾语＋原形，blend in表示融入背景。"},{"bid":"RW463:2","answer":"makes","primary_point":"G11","primary_name":"宾语、补语与使役结构","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"makes it a camouflage champion为make＋宾语＋名词补语。"},{"bid":"RW463:3","answer":"based","primary_point":"G07","primary_name":"分词修饰与逻辑主语","secondary_points":["C04"],"evidence":"based on its patterns为过去分词结构，表示筑巢选择以自身花纹为依据。"},{"bid":"RW463:4","answer":"both","primary_point":"G10","primary_name":"并列层级与共享成分","secondary_points":["P03"],"evidence":"both within a habitat and at a fine scale为both...and...并列范围。"}]},{"practice_id":"T044","source":"RW147","type":"RW","question_id":147,"title":"Sydney","page":109,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Sydney is becoming effective in making the best of its limited available unconstrained land. Sydney is suitable for integrating suitable business, office, residential, retail and other development in accessible locations so as to maximise public transport 【 patron, patronizing, patronize, patrons, patronage 】 and encourage walking and cycling. Also this city can reduce the 【 consumption, consumed, consume, consuming, consumable 】 of land for housing and associated urban development on the urban fringe. For the proposed mixed business, mixed use and business park areas, there was no employment data available for 【 comparison, compared, compare, comparing, comparable 】 areas. It is also concluded that lack of housing supply will affect 【 affording, afford, affordable, afforded, affordability 】 in Sydney.","answers":["patronage","consumption","comparable","affordability"],"options":["patron, patronizing, patronize, patrons, patronage","consumption, consumed, consume, consuming, consumable","comparison, compared, compare, comparing, comparable","affording, afford, affordable, afforded, affordability"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW147:1","answer":"patronage","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["S03","S01"],"evidence":"maximise public transport patronage表示提高公共交通使用/客流，patronage为名词；patron指顾客个人，其他为动词/分词。"},{"bid":"RW147:2","answer":"consumption","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"reduce the consumption of land，the后名词consumption；其余词形不作宾语核心。"},{"bid":"RW147:3","answer":"comparable","primary_point":"F01","primary_name":"句法槽位与词性","secondary_points":["C02","Q01","S01"],"evidence":"data available for comparable areas，需要形容词修饰areas，表示可比较地区；comparison也可作名词定语但comparable直接表达性质，其他词形不合。"},{"bid":"RW147:4","answer":"affordability","primary_point":"F01","primary_name":"句法槽位与词性","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"affect affordability in Sydney，affordability名词作affect宾语，指住房负担能力；其余词形不合。"}]},{"practice_id":"T045","source":"RW474","type":"RW","question_id":474,"title":"Funerary Violin","page":352,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"In the 250 years of its active evolution, funerary violin moved from the formal to the personal. It is clear from the earliest 【 memory, recall, accounts, count 】 of the form that its role during the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries was largely heraldic, to 【 exemplify, simplify, modify, specify 】 the continuity of the social 【 infrastructure, discrimination, structure, frustration 】 . The few works that have survived from this period are often 【 surprisingly, regularly, expectedly, normally 】 unemotional and at times overtly grandiose.","answers":["accounts","exemplify","structure","surprisingly"],"options":["memory, recall, accounts, count","exemplify, simplify, modify, specify","infrastructure, discrimination, structure, frustration","surprisingly, regularly, expectedly, normally"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW474:1","answer":"accounts","primary_point":"C06","primary_name":"名词＋介词配价","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"earliest accounts of the form指关于丧葬小提琴形式的最早记载。"},{"bid":"RW474:2","answer":"exemplify","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["C01","S01"],"evidence":"role was to exemplify continuity中不定式说明功能：体现社会结构延续。"},{"bid":"RW474:3","answer":"structure","primary_point":"C03","primary_name":"名词＋名词术语","secondary_points":["S04"],"evidence":"social structure为社会结构，与heraldic公共象征功能相配。"},{"bid":"RW474:4","answer":"surprisingly","primary_point":"F05","primary_name":"副词位置与修饰目标","secondary_points":["D04"],"evidence":"surprisingly unemotional表示与丧葬音乐预期相反地缺少情感。"}]},{"practice_id":"T046","source":"R215","type":"R","question_id":215,"title":"Moth","page":250,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"Why are moths fatally attracted to the light? 【 One solution 】 is the old glib theory that the moths are trying to use the flame to navigate. 【 This explanation 】 does not tell us, 【 however 】 , why it is that in many species only males are thus attracted, and in a few, only females. 【 What's more 】 , if moths need to navigate, they must be from a migrating species. 【 Yet 】 most of the time such moths are not migrating. Indeed most species do not migrate at all and thus have no need of navigation.","answers":["One solution","This explanation","however","What's more","Yet"],"options":["One solution","This explanation","however","What's more","Yet"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R215:1","answer":"One solution","primary_point":"D01","primary_name":"代词指代与替代","secondary_points":["S02"],"evidence":"One solution承接why问句并提出一种旧理论，语义可理解，但one answer/explanation更自然；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R215:2","answer":"This explanation","primary_point":"D01","primary_name":"代词指代与替代","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"This explanation回指前句导航理论，后接does not tell us指出解释漏洞；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R215:3","answer":"however","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"however置于插入位置，两侧逗号隔开，引出该理论无法解释性别差异；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R215:4","answer":"What's more","primary_point":"D05","primary_name":"补充、递进与时序","secondary_points":["Q02"],"evidence":"What’s more递进补充第二个反证：多数飞蛾并未迁徙；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"},{"bid":"R215:5","answer":"Yet","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["Q02"],"evidence":"Yet引转折，理论要求迁徙，但事实上多数此时并不迁徙；原词池缺失，不能证明唯一。"}]},{"practice_id":"T047","source":"RW497","type":"RW","question_id":497,"title":"Bones","page":369,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Bones also protect the organs in our bodies. The skull protects the brain and forms the shape of the face. The spinal cord, a pathway for messages between the brain and the body, is protected by the backbone, or spinal column. The ribs form a cage that shelters 【 a, that, our, the 】 heart and lungs, and the pelvis helps protect the bladder, part of the intestines, and in women, the reproductive organs. Bones are made up of a framework of a protein called collagen , with a mineral called calcium phosphate that makes the framework hard and strong. Bones store calcium and release some into the bloodstream when it's needed by other parts of the body. The amounts of certain vitamins and minerals that you eat, especially vitamin D and calcium, directly affect how much calcium is stored in the bones. Joints are where 【 that, which, one, two 】 bones meet. They make the skeleton flexible — without them, movement would be impossible. Joints allow our bodies to move in many ways. Some joints open and close like a hinge (such as knees and elbows), whereas others allow for more complicated movement — a shoulder or hip joint, for example, allows for backward, forward, sideways, and rotating movement. Joints are classified by their range of movement: Immovable, or fibrous, joints don't move. The dome of the skull, for example, is made of bony plates, which move slightly during birth and then fuse together as the skull finishes growing. Between the edges of these plates are links, or joints, of fibrous tissue. Fibrous joints also hold the teeth in the jawbone. Partially movable, or cartilaginous, joints move a little. They are linked by cartilage, as in the spine. Each of the vertebrae in the spine moves in relation to the one above and below it, and together these movements give the spine its flexibility. Freely movable, or synovial (pronounced: sih-NO-vee-ul), joints move in many directions. The 【 whole, entire, individual, main 】 joints of the body — such as those found at the hip, shoulders, elbows, knees, wrists, and ankles — are freely movable. They are filled with synovial fluid, which acts as a lubricant to help the joints move easily. 【 All, Two, One, Three 】 kinds of freely movable joints play a big part in voluntary movement: Hinge joints allow movement in one direction, as seen in the knees and elbows. Pivot joints allow a rotating or twisting motion, like that of the head moving from side to side. Ball-and-socket joints allow the greatest freedom 【 with, to, during, of 】 movement. The hips and shoulders have this type of joint, in which the round end of a long bone fits into the hollow of another bone.","answers":["the","two","main","Three","of"],"options":["a, that, our, the","that, which, one, two","whole, entire, individual, main","All, Two, One, Three","with, to, during, of"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW497:1","answer":"the","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“a, that, our, the”后，“the”在语境“the backbone, or spinal column. The ribs form a cage that shelters the heart and lungs, and the pelvis helps protect the bladder, part of”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW497:2","answer":"two","primary_point":"Q02","primary_name":"数量词与比例","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“that, which, one, two”后，“two”在语境“affect how much calcium is stored in the bones. Joints are where two bones meet. They make the skeleton flexible — without them, movement would”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW497:3","answer":"main","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"逐项比较“whole, entire, individual, main”后，“main”在语境“Freely movable, or synovial (pronounced: sih-NO-vee-ul), joints move in many directions. The main joints of the body — such as those found at the hip,”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW497:4","answer":"Three","primary_point":"Q02","primary_name":"数量词与比例","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"逐项比较“All, Two, One, Three”后，“Three”在语境“fluid, which acts as a lubricant to help the joints move easily. Three kinds of freely movable joints play a big part in voluntary movement:”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"},{"bid":"RW497:5","answer":"of","primary_point":"P01","primary_name":"时间、空间与方向介词","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"逐项比较“with, to, during, of”后，“of”在语境“head moving from side to side. Ball-and-socket joints allow the greatest freedom of movement. The hips and shoulders have this type of joint, in which”中由句法形式、搭配或全文逻辑获得有效排他证据。"}]},{"practice_id":"T048","source":"RW31","type":"RW","question_id":31,"title":"Early Humans","page":21,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Early humans were hunter-gatherers, roaming from place to place, but their movements were controlled by the need for water. When humans 【 start, have started, starting, started 】 to grow food and established permanent settlements, water was needed for crops and animals as well as for people, 【 because, so, thus, thereby 】 settlements have always grown up near reliable sources of water. Most major towns lie on the banks of rivers, or, where there are no streams or rivers, settlements exist where underground water can be reached by digging wells. The management of water resources has a 【 meticulous study, moderate change, brief existence, long history 】 . The oldest known dam in the world was constructed in Egypt about 5000 years ago, and was used for storing drinking and irrigation water. Farmers in Arabia at this time used the craters of extinct volcanoes as storage tanks for irrigation water and dug deep wells for their drinking water. Excavated ruins in India of similar antiquity retain the remains of water supply and drainage systems, 【 as, what, which, whatever 】 included baths and swimming pools.","answers":["started","so","long history","which"],"options":["start, have started, starting, started","because, so, thus, thereby","meticulous study, moderate change, brief existence, long history","as, what, which, whatever"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW31:1","answer":"started","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["G03","G10","G01"],"evidence":"早期人类历史叙述，started与established并列过去时；starting缺有限谓语，start/have started与此过去叙事不一致。"},{"bid":"RW31:2","answer":"so","primary_point":"D03","primary_name":"因果与结果","secondary_points":["G01","S05","S01"],"evidence":"人畜农作物需水是定居点靠水的原因，so连接结果分句；thus也可表示因此，但标准书面句法应避免只以逗号加thus连接独立句。because反转因果，thereby不能直接连接此完整分句。"},{"bid":"RW31:3","answer":"long history","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["D05","S03","S04"],"evidence":"后面5000年前的水坝与同时代水利遗迹说明long history，brief existence方向反；meticulous study/moderate change不能概括久远实践的时间跨度。"},{"bid":"RW31:4","answer":"which","primary_point":"G08","primary_name":"关系从句与缺口","secondary_points":["C03","D06","D01"],"evidence":"逗号后which included回指water supply and drainage systems，非限制性关系从句；what/whatever不能直接回指已有先行词，as在此不是常用列举构造。"}]},{"practice_id":"T049","source":"RW41","type":"RW","question_id":41,"title":"Transitions in Britain","page":28,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"The transitions which occurred in Britain around 100 BC, and after 43 AD (when the Roman Army 【 purported, pursued, enlightened, invaded 】 Britain) represent the key points of socio-economic trend in Britain's past. During the first century BC, the traditional communal form of life 【 withdrew, shaped, awarded, shifted 】 rapidly to a world where certain individuals 【 having become, became, become, becoming 】 more important. During the first century AD, Britain became fully a part of the Roman Empire.","answers":["invaded","shifted","became"],"options":["purported, pursued, enlightened, invaded","withdrew, shaped, awarded, shifted","having become, became, become, becoming"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW41:1","answer":"invaded","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"Roman Army对Britain的行动，后文became part of Empire支持invaded入侵；purported声称、pursued追逐、enlightened启发不描述征服。"},{"bid":"RW41:2","answer":"shifted","primary_point":"S02","primary_name":"近义词精确辨析","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"communal life shifted to a world of individuals为社会形式转变，shift to；withdrew退出、shaped塑造、awarded授予都不成此转向配价。"},{"bid":"RW41:3","answer":"became","primary_point":"G01","primary_name":"句子边界与有限谓语","secondary_points":["G02","S07"],"evidence":"where后主语certain individuals需有限谓语became，first century BC限定过去；having become/becoming为非限定结构，become一般现在不符历史叙述。"}]},{"practice_id":"T050","source":"R488","type":"R","question_id":488,"title":"Parental Income","page":543,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"In England it is well known that access to university, on average, varies substantially by the levels of parental income and that students from poorer families access different types of universities than those from wealthier backgrounds. However, the question of whether graduates’ earnings vary 【 according to 】 their socioeconomic backgrounds amongst graduates attending similar universities and taking the same subject has remained poorly understood, 【 thus far 】 limited by data availability. Our unique administrative database offers substantial advantages 【 in addressing 】 this crucial question. The findings are also relevant for myriad other issues that benefit from better information on 【 variation 】 in graduates’ earnings, including: students’ choices of subjects and institutions; better information for schools 【 to help 】 advise and guide students whilst at school; and the operation and cost of the higher education finance system.","answers":["according to","thus far","in addressing","variation","to help"],"options":["according to","thus far","in addressing","variation","to help"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R488:1","answer":"according to","primary_point":"P02","primary_name":"介词短语与从句连接","secondary_points":["C04"],"evidence":"给定词“according to”与语境“those from wealthier backgrounds. However, the question of whether graduates’ earnings vary according to their socioeconomic backgrounds amongst graduates attending similar universities and taking the same”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R488:2","answer":"thus far","primary_point":"F02","primary_name":"词族与派生形式","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"给定词“thus far”与语境“attending similar universities and taking the same subject has remained poorly understood, thus far limited by data availability. Our unique administrative database offers substantial advantages”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R488:3","answer":"in addressing","primary_point":"P02","primary_name":"介词短语与从句连接","secondary_points":["C04"],"evidence":"给定词“in addressing”与语境“limited by data availability. Our unique administrative database offers substantial advantages in addressing this crucial question. The findings are also relevant for myriad other issues”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R488:4","answer":"variation","primary_point":"S04","primary_name":"定义、类别与例项","secondary_points":["F03"],"evidence":"给定词“variation”与语境“also relevant for myriad other issues that benefit from better information on variation in graduates’ earnings, including: students’ choices of subjects and institutions; better information”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"},{"bid":"R488:5","answer":"to help","primary_point":"G05","primary_name":"不定式及动词补语","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"给定词“to help”与语境“earnings, including: students’ choices of subjects and institutions; better information for schools to help advise and guide students whilst at school; and the operation and cost”的句法槽位、搭配及上下文方向相容；R原材料无干扰词池，因此不认证唯一性。"}]},{"practice_id":"T051","source":"RW398","type":"RW","question_id":398,"title":"Reading","page":294,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Reading is an active process, not a 【 passive, positive, objective, proactive 】 one. We always read within a 【 explicit, implicit, specific, general 】 context and this affects what we notice and what seems to matter. We always have a purpose in reading a text, and this will shape how we 【 approach, close, preempt, nettle 】 it. Our purpose and background knowledge will also 【 conclude, determine, undermined, detect 】 the strategies we use to read the text.","answers":["passive","specific","approach","determine"],"options":["passive, positive, objective, proactive","explicit, implicit, specific, general","approach, close, preempt, nettle","conclude, determine, undermined, detect"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW398:1","answer":"passive","primary_point":"D04","primary_name":"转折、让步与反驳","secondary_points":["C02"],"evidence":"active process, not a passive one构成直接反义对照；positive/objective/proactive都不与active形成此处定义反义。"},{"bid":"RW398:2","answer":"specific","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S07"],"evidence":"a specific context表示每次阅读发生在具体情境；general与后文个人目的不符，explicit/implicit只是情境属性。"},{"bid":"RW398:3","answer":"approach","primary_point":"S06","primary_name":"一词多义、比喻与专业义","secondary_points":["C01"],"evidence":"approach a text在此指处理/阅读文本；close、preempt、nettle均不合对象与语境。"},{"bid":"RW398:4","answer":"determine","primary_point":"C01","primary_name":"动词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["G03"],"evidence":"purpose and knowledge determine strategies表示二者决定策略；复数并列主语用原形，其他动词含义或词形不合。"}]},{"practice_id":"T052","source":"R14","type":"R","question_id":14,"title":"City Design","page":16,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"The way we design our cities needs a serious rethink. After thousands of years of progress in urban development, we 【 plateaued 】 some 60 years ago. Cities are not safer, healthier, more efficient, or more 【 equitable 】 . They are getting worse on these measures. The statistics on chronic disease, rising road tolls and congestion in our urban environments paint a 【 bleak 】 future. The clues to why lie in how we think about and design our cities.","answers":["plateaued","equitable","bleak"],"options":["plateaued","equitable","bleak"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R14:1","answer":"plateaued","primary_point":"S03","primary_name":"变化方向与程度","secondary_points":["G02","S06"],"evidence":"After progress后说60年前plateaued达到停滞平台，后面not safer及getting worse解释进步停顿；ago定位过去式。"},{"bid":"R14:2","answer":"equitable","primary_point":"G10","primary_name":"并列层级与共享成分","secondary_points":["Q01","F01"],"evidence":"safer、healthier、more efficient与more equitable平行比较城市公平性，equitable为形容词，不是equal的简单拼写变形。"},{"bid":"R14:3","answer":"bleak","primary_point":"C02","primary_name":"形容词＋名词搭配","secondary_points":["S03"],"evidence":"disease、road tolls、congestion与getting worse支持paint a bleak future描绘黯淡前景，bleak不是积极改善。"}]},{"practice_id":"T053","source":"R356","type":"R","question_id":356,"title":"Statistical Theory","page":397,"mode":"语境回忆；原干扰词池缺失，不认证唯一性","passage":"Social reforms are normally 【 initiated 】 as a result of statistical analyses of factors such as crime rates and poverty levels etc. Large-scale population can result from projections devised by statisticians. Manufacturers can provide better products at lower costs by 【 using 】 statistical control tools, 【 such 】 as control charts. Diseases are controlled through analyses designed to anticipate epidemics. Endangered species of fish and other wildlife are protected through regulations and laws that react to statistical estimates of changing population sizes. And, 【 through 】 statistical analysis of fatality rates, legislators can better justify laws, such as those governing air pollution, auto inspections, seat belt and airbag use, and drunk driving.","answers":["initiated","using","such","through"],"options":["initiated","using","such","through"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"R356:1","answer":"initiated","primary_point":"G04","primary_name":"主动被动与助动词链","secondary_points":["D03"],"evidence":"social reforms are initiated为一般现在时被动，as a result of引出启动改革的依据。"},{"bid":"R356:2","answer":"using","primary_point":"G06","primary_name":"动名词与介词后动作","secondary_points":["S05"],"evidence":"by using statistical control tools中by后接动名词，表示实现手段。"},{"bid":"R356:3","answer":"such","primary_point":"D06","primary_name":"条件、例外与举例","secondary_points":["C08"],"evidence":"such as引出control charts这一具体例项。"},{"bid":"R356:4","answer":"through","primary_point":"S05","primary_name":"过程阶段与结果","secondary_points":["P01"],"evidence":"through statistical analysis说明论证立法的手段或途径。"}]},{"practice_id":"T054","source":"RW126","type":"RW","question_id":126,"title":"Love of Reading","page":92,"mode":"原始选项训练","passage":"Many parents want their children to grow up with a love of reading. However, recent research 【 shown, has shown, show, showing 】 that children nowadays spend far more of their time using their phones or computers than reading books. Of course, technology brings children many advantages, but books are 【 so, as, very, such 】 important as computers. For instance, when children read storybooks, they imagine the characters and practise their language skills, too. Many British schools run an event called World Book Day. This event 【 differs, defers, aims, disagrees 】 to promote reading to pupils using various fun activities. Some pupils come to school in costumes inspired by their favourite book. Other schools organise World Book Day activities where pupils create music, art or plays about books. But it's also important for children to read at home, too. At the moment, 【 very few, a little, a few, less 】 parents spend time reading with their children regularly. Unfortunately, this means that these children are missing an opportunity to develop the reading habit at an early age.","answers":["has shown","as","aims","very few"],"options":["shown, has shown, show, showing","so, as, very, such","differs, defers, aims, disagrees","very few, a little, a few, less"],"blank_map":[{"bid":"RW126:1","answer":"has shown","primary_point":"G02","primary_name":"时态与时间参照","secondary_points":["F03","D03","S05"],"evidence":"recent research has shown that...，research不可数作单数，recent研究结果影响现在用现在完成；shown缺助动词，show数不合，showing缺谓语。"},{"bid":"RW126:2","answer":"as","primary_point":"Q01","primary_name":"比较结构与比较对象","secondary_points":[],"evidence":"books are as important as computers，同级比较首个as空缺；so/very/such不形成as...as。"},{"bid":"RW126:3","answer":"aims","primary_point":"C08","primary_name":"固定表达与学术词块","secondary_points":["G05","S01"],"evidence":"event aims to promote reading，aim to do表示活动目的；differs/defers/disagrees需其他介词且不表推广目的。"},{"bid":"RW126:4","answer":"very few","primary_point":"F03","primary_name":"可数性与限定词","secondary_points":["S01"],"evidence":"very few parents表示极少家长，parents可数复数；a few表示有一些且语气不支持Unfortunately，little/less不修饰可数复数。"}]}],"stats":{"pointCount":44,"questionCount":54,"blankCount":295}};
